), A("ts1")))), S2(A("FailureOccurredAtTimestamp"), S1(S2(A("f1"), A("ts2")))), S2(A("FailureIsCausedByViolation"), PHI()), S2(A("DerivationRuleIsProvidedByConstraint"), S1(S2(A("dr1"), A("c1")))), S2(A("DerivationRuleProducesFactType"), S3(S2(A("dr1"), A("ftc")), S2(A("dr2"), A("fta")), S2(A("dr3"), A("ftb")))), S2(A("DerivationRuleHasAntecedentFactType"), S2(S2(A("dr1"), A("fta")), S2(A("dr2"), A("ftb")))), S2(A("FactIsOfFactType"), S2(S2(A("fx"), A("fta")), S2(A("fz"), A("otherft"))))), S2(S2(A("FactFillsRoleUsesResource"), S4(S2(S2(A("fa"), A("ra1")), A("va")), S2(S2(A("fa"), A("ra2")), A("vb")), S2(S2(A("fb"), A("rb1")), A("vb")), S2(S2(A("fb"), A("rb2")), A("vc")))), S2(A("RoleIsUsedInReadingHasPosition"), S4(S2(S2(A("ra1"), A("rda")), N(1)), S2(S2(A("ra2"), A("rda")), N(2)), S2(S2(A("rb1"), A("rdb")), N(1)), S2(S2(A("rb2"), A("rdb")), N(2)))))))))))),

"DOMAIN REACHES DOMAIN RUNS PARENT TO CHILD. core.md: Domain1 reaches Domain2 iff Domain2 is contained in Domain1, reaching being data addressing, a parent into its children, as AREST.tex sub-tenancy says. The fixture holds dom1 contained in dom2 and dom2 contained in dom3, so the derived reaches are dom2 to dom1, dom3 to dom2 and dom3 to dom1; core.md derives no child-to-parent rows.",
