                  S4(S2(A("Start Date"), A("a.1")), S2(A("End Date"), A("b.1")), S2(A("Amount"), A("c.1")), S2(A("Customer"), A("d.1"))),
                  S3(S2(A("Start Date"), A("date")), S2(A("End Date"), A("date")), S2(A("Amount"), A("decimal")))))),
          K(S2(A("v2"), A("v3")))))),
"test:decided_unfilled holds decide:ur_rows to literal rows, each span numbered as <sequence>.<position>. u1 is a uniqueness over a.1 (1.1); s1 a subset of a.1 (1.1) in b.1 (2.1). s2 is a subset that kept its sequence 1 alone, s3 one that kept its sequence 2 alone, e1 an equality of a.1, a.2 with b.1 (1.1, 1.2, 2.1), e2 one of a.1 with b.1, b.2 (1.1, 2.1, 2.2), m1 a mandatory over c.1 and c.3 (1.1, 1.3), x1 an exclusion that spans nothing, v1 a value comparison of one role, and d1 a deontic whose one span has no numbers. So m1 (no 1.2), s3 (no sequence 1, and no 1.1 under 2.1), e2 (no 1.2 under 2.2), e1 (no 2.2 though sequence 2 has 2.1), s2 (one sequence) and v1 (one Role) answer, each once where theta:dedup keeps it, and u1, s1 and d1 do not, nor x1, which spans no Role and is the obligation`s that each Constraint spans some Role. Run first against an answer without e1, it failed (decided-unfilled -> F).",
DEF("test:decided_unfilled",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("decide:ur_rows"),
             K(S4(S(S2(A("u1"), A("UC")), S2(A("s1"), A("SS")), S2(A("s2"), A("SS")), S2(A("s3"), A("SS")), S2(A("e1"), A("EQ")), S2(A("e2"), A("EQ")), S2(A("m1"), A("MC")), S2(A("x1"), A("XC")), S2(A("v1"), A("VC")), S2(A("d1"), A("DO_pop"))),
                  S(S2(A("u1"), A("a.1")), S2(A("s1"), A("a.1")), S2(A("s1"), A("b.1")), S2(A("s2"), A("a.1")), S2(A("s3"), A("b.1")), S2(A("e1"), A("a.1")), S2(A("e1"), A("a.2")), S2(A("e1"), A("b.1")), S2(A("e2"), A("a.1")), S2(A("e2"), A("b.1")), S2(A("e2"), A("b.2")), S2(A("m1"), A("c.1")), S2(A("m1"), A("c.3")), S2(A("v1"), A("a.1")), S2(A("d1"), A("a.1"))),
                  S(S2(A("u1.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("s1.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("s1.b.1"), N(2)), S2(A("s2.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("s3.b.1"), N(2)), S2(A("e1.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("e1.a.2"), N(1)), S2(A("e1.b.1"), N(2)), S2(A("e2.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("e2.b.1"), N(2)), S2(A("e2.b.2"), N(2)), S2(A("m1.c.1"), N(1)), S2(A("m1.c.3"), N(1)), S2(A("v1.a.1"), N(1))),
                  S(S2(A("u1.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("s1.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("s1.b.1"), N(1)), S2(A("s2.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("s3.b.1"), N(1)), S2(A("e1.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("e1.a.2"), N(2)), S2(A("e1.b.1"), N(1)), S2(A("e2.a.1"), N(1)), S2(A("e2.b.1"), N(1)), S2(A("e2.b.2"), N(2)), S2(A("m1.c.1"), N(1)), S2(A("m1.c.3"), N(3)), S2(A("v1.a.1"), N(1)))))),
          K(S6(A("m1"), A("s3"), A("e2"), A("e1"), A("s2"), A("v1")))))),
"test:decided_moore_mealy holds decide:mm_rows to literal rows. Machine m1 defines a and b, and p1 is performed in a, so m1 has a state action; t1 goes to b with p2 performed during it, and p2 is not performed in b; t2 goes to b with p3, which b performs. Machine m2 has no state action, and t3 goes to d with p4. So t1 answers, and neither t2 nor t3. Run first against an answer of t3, it failed (decided-moore-mealy -> F).",
DEF("test:decided_moore_mealy",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("decide:mm_rows"),
             K(S5(S2(S2(A("p1"), A("a")), S2(A("p3"), A("b"))),
                  S4(S2(A("a"), A("m1")), S2(A("b"), A("m1")), S2(A("c"), A("m2")), S2(A("d"), A("m2"))),
                  S3(S2(A("p2"), A("t1")), S2(A("p3"), A("t2")), S2(A("p4"), A("t3"))),
                  S3(S2(A("t1"), A("m1")), S2(A("t2"), A("m1")), S2(A("t3"), A("m2"))),
                  S3(S2(A("t1"), A("b")), S2(A("t2"), A("b")), S2(A("t3"), A("d")))))),
          K(S1(A("t1")))))),
"test:decided_cycle_exit holds decide:ce_rows to literal rows <reaches, exits, to, defined in, sub-machines>. In m1, a and b reach each other and both reach c, which reaches neither, and t3 goes from b to c: the cycle {a, b} has an exit. In m2, x and y reach each other and every transition stays between them; in m3, z goes to itself. m4 is the sub-machine of o4, a Status of m5, and defines p and q, which reach each other, and t9, which m5 defines from o4 to r, exits m4 from outside and so leaves p and q (decide:ce_ext), so the cycle {p, q} has an exit. So m2 and m3 answer, and m1 and m4 do not. If the exit from outside is not counted, m4 answers as support.auto.dev`s Open did; and the composite o4 is no machine, so decide:ce_ext reads the sub-machine fact.",
DEF("test:decided_cycle_exit",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("decide:ce_rows"),
             K(S5(S(S3(A("a"), A("b"), A("m1")), S3(A("b"), A("a"), A("m1")), S3(A("a"), A("a"), A("m1")), S3(A("b"), A("b"), A("m1")), S3(A("a"), A("c"), A("m1")), S3(A("b"), A("c"), A("m1")), S3(A("x"), A("y"), A("m2")), S3(A("y"), A("x"), A("m2")), S3(A("x"), A("x"), A("m2")), S3(A("y"), A("y"), A("m2")), S3(A("z"), A("z"), A("m3")), S3(A("p"), A("q"), A("m4")), S3(A("q"), A("p"), A("m4")), S3(A("p"), A("p"), A("m4")), S3(A("q"), A("q"), A("m4")), S3(A("o4"), A("r"), A("m5"))),
                  S9(S3(A("t1"), A("a"), A("m1")), S3(A("t2"), A("b"), A("m1")), S3(A("t3"), A("b"), A("m1")), S3(A("t4"), A("x"), A("m2")), S3(A("t5"), A("y"), A("m2")), S3(A("t6"), A("z"), A("m3")), S3(A("t7"), A("p"), A("m4")), S3(A("t8"), A("q"), A("m4")), S3(A("t9"), A("o4"), A("m5"))),
                  S9(S2(A("t1"), A("b")), S2(A("t2"), A("a")), S2(A("t3"), A("c")), S2(A("t4"), A("y")), S2(A("t5"), A("x")), S2(A("t6"), A("z")), S2(A("t7"), A("q")), S2(A("t8"), A("p")), S2(A("t9"), A("r"))),
                  S3(S2(A("p"), A("m4")), S2(A("q"), A("m4")), S2(A("o4"), A("m5"))),
                  S1(S2(A("o4"), A("m4")))))),
          K(S2(A("m2"), A("m3")))))),
"test:decided_ssrf_resolved holds the resolved half to literal rows: r1 resolved to 10.0.0.5 and to a public address, r2 only to a public one, r3 to [::1]'s address, so r1 and r3 answer; and perform:blocked_in answers the first blocked address of a list, 192.168.1.9, and the empty string for a list with none.",
