               S2(S2(A("FT1"), A("FT1.1")), S2(A("FT1"), A("FT1.2")))))),
       K(S1(A("w2")))))),
"THE DECIDED VIOLATIONS A STORE HOLDS, to read. test:decided_witness renders each row cmd:dec_viols answers, and `witness` prints them; test:decided_clean is what the witness agrees with. A deontic violation is the work list, not a refusal, so this is no law of the report: the metamodel may hold some, and they are its to fix.",
DEF("test:decided_witness",
    S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("system:show")), A("cmd:dec_viols")), K(PHI()))),
DEF("test:decided_clean",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("cmd:dec_viols"))),
"test:decided_bound holds the store to its own bindings: some constraint is decided by a predicate, and every such predicate resolves through cmd:dec_sym to a decider this file lists. A binding with a misspelled Symbol Name, a Module Path other than 'arest', or no Predicate facts at all decides nothing, and this is where that shows.",
DEF("test:decided_bound",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("and"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintIsDecidedByPredicate")), A("id")))),
          S5(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"),
             S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("cmd:dec_sym"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), N(2))), K(A(""))))),
             A("distr"),
             S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintIsDecidedByPredicate")), A("id"))), A("id")))))),

"<the answer of main:assert_all, the page, the store before> to the answer narrowed by the values the write touched, found whether or not it has a violation to narrow: what main:ab_scope answers, and case:an-asserts-scope-is-the-whole-scope-with-or-without-a-violation holds the two equal.",
DEF("test:ab_scope_all",
    S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), K(A("refused")))), N(1),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("main:ab_scope2"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:ab_mine"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), A("main:ab_svals"))))))),
"test:orient_required: orient re-orients an agent (`Object Type Instance is required orientation.`, instances.md). The fixture is the store the law is handed with an App or-app whose navigable Domains are or-alpha and or-beta, each a Domain with a Description, and three instances of LawOrNote: or-n1 and or-n2 belong to or-alpha and or-n3 to or-beta; or-n1 and or-n2 are required orientation; or-n2 is currently in Applied, which the Domain Change machine declares terminal. or-n1 has a title and a kind, and states the practice or-p1. orient on or-app answers three rows: first or-n1, tagged with the fact type that put it there and followed by what get answers for it, its facts and its links with their values; then the two Descriptions. No row is a belongs-to-Domain row, or-n2 is absent because it is retired, and or-n3, live but not required, is absent because orient answers the Descriptions and the required orientation and nothing else of a Domain (Function `orient`, resolution.md). orient on or-beta answers its Description alone. test:or_add puts a population back as a top-level cell with the fixture rows in front of what the store holds of it.",
DEF("test:or_add",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("store:cl_put"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"),
                S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)),
                   S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), N(1)))))),
          N(1)))),
DEF("test:or_store",
    S9(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("state:fts"), S3(
             S5(A("LawOrNoteHasTitle"), S2(A("LawOrNote"), A("Title")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(),
                S3(S2(A("or-n1"), A("keep the law first")), S2(A("or-n2"), A("a retired note")), S2(A("or-n3"), A("a plain note")))),
             S5(A("LawOrNoteHasKind"), S2(A("LawOrNote"), A("Kind")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(),
                S1(S2(A("or-n1"), A("rule")))),
             S5(A("LawOrNoteStatesPractice"), S2(A("LawOrNote"), A("Practice")), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), PHI(),
                S1(S2(A("or-n1"), A("or-p1"))))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("state:otmeta"), S1(S2(A("LawOrNote"), A("entity"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:or_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("AppHasNavigableDomain"), S2(S2(A("or-app"), A("or-alpha")), S2(A("or-app"), A("or-beta"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:or_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S2(S2(A("or-alpha"), A("Domain")), S2(A("or-beta"), A("Domain"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:or_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("FunctionHasDescription"), S2(S2(A("or-alpha"), A("Alpha holds the notes an agent reads first.")), S2(A("or-beta"), A("Beta holds the rest."))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:or_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceBelongsToDomain"), S3(S2(A("or-n1"), A("or-alpha")), S2(A("or-n2"), A("or-alpha")), S2(A("or-n3"), A("or-beta"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:or_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsRequiredOrientation"), S2(S1(A("or-n1")), S1(A("or-n2"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:or_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus"), S1(S2(A("or-n2"), A("Applied"))))))))),
DEF("test:or_answers",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("orient"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("or-app")), A("id"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("orient"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("or-beta")), A("id")))),
       A("test:or_store"))),
DEF("test:or_first",
    K(S5(A("or-alpha"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsRequiredOrientation"), A("or-n1"),
         S2(A("facts"), S2(S2(A("LawOrNoteHasTitle"), A("keep the law first")), S2(A("LawOrNoteHasKind"), A("rule")))),
         S2(A("links"), S1(S4(A("LawOrNoteStatesPractice"), S1(A("or-n1")), N(1), S1(A("or-p1")))))))),
DEF("test:orient_required",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S9(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), N(1)), K(N(3)))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), N(1)), K(A("F")),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), A("test:or_first")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("or-alpha"), A("FunctionHasDescription"), A("Alpha holds the notes an agent reads first."))), N(1))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("or-beta"), A("FunctionHasDescription"), A("Beta holds the rest."))), N(1))),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("theta:flatten"),
          S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceBelongsToDomain"), A("FunctionBelongsToDomain"))))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI()))),
          N(1)),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("theta:flatten"),
          S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), N(3), K(S2(A("or-n2"), A("or-n3"))))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI()))),
          N(1)),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(S1(S3(A("or-beta"), A("FunctionHasDescription"), A("Beta holds the rest.")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), N(2)), K(N(1))))),
       A("test:or_answers")))),

"THE STORE-WIDE INDUCTION IS OUT OF THE REPORT. test:induce's first conjunct applied induce to every declared derived fact type of the store under test, rebuilding candidate rules from every pair of the store's binary fact types and checking that their union covered each declared population -- 3.18 million induce:join_cands calls in the first 90 s of the support report over its compiled map, the whole of that report's cost once the map was compiled. Nothing in the by-hand process does that: a derivation is declared and the report checks that the declared rule evaluates to its population (test:derive, the step-product laws) and that the map agrees with NORMA. The induce function keeps its fixtures below, which are its test, and stays the cli's induce action; the report no longer runs it over the store, and induce:declared, the declared heads that conjunct alone read, went with it (the unreachable-set law named it).",

DEF("test:induce",
