"AND A FUNCTION THE MODEL CANNOT FULLY ADDRESS IS A CALL NOBODY CAN MAKE. test:callable holds when every Function backed by an External System has a method, a system with a URL, and a path. It is VACUOUS on a store that federates with nothing -- the base store -- so it costs nothing there, and it is the detector for a Function like sendSupportEmail with its system, its URL and its path and NO METHOD, which nothing else reports. The headers are not checked here because whether a call needs one is the External System's business, not the Function's; that is a second law over ExternalSystemAuthenticatesWithHeader and it is owed.",
