"VERB SHAPES DECLARED. An Operation that declares what it accepts declares it once and what it yields once, and if lambda serves it as a verb (it is a lambda cell) the accepted shape is one main:verb_shapes knows, or main:verb_pair hands it the default pair and the answer is luck. An Operation with no accepts row is a shape the model calls unsettled (resolution.md), and the law says nothing of it; mcp:verb_names is every overridable and registrable Operation, twinnable definitions and host primitives included, which is why the row count is the test and not the name. The operand is the store cells.",

