"WHICH CELLS DOES NOTHING REACH? Correct code with no caller is this codebase s recurring defect, not an instance of one: ast:File built FILE for a law while the runtime never did, rmap:ddl_table and rmap:ddl_order walked a schema nobody asked for, and all four links(e) defects were of this kind. Nothing detected it, which is why it accumulated. AREST.tex Corollary 8 puts the host boundary inside DEFS as a restriction, and Corollary 1 makes graph questions over D decidable by restriction, so reachability is a question lambda can ask about itself. theta:flatten is ONE level deep, so the atom walk below is recursive; the whole edge extraction is about two seconds over 123k atoms, which is affordable inside a report that already takes minutes.",
"A MACHINE WITH NO INSTANCES ANSWERED BY DYING. main:links_of already refused a noun with no machine; it had no sibling refusal for a machine with no entities, and system:links_of indexes a status list it assumes is non-empty. So all three machines the composed store declares -- Schema Design, Relational Mapping, Domain Change, none of which has an instance -- made links_of throw, which is every fresh app on its first request. No case caught it because every links case supplies its status rows as non-empty LITERALS, which is the defect this law exists to close: an algebra proven over a literal says nothing about the store.",
