"test:carried_subject holds the places the stored schema`s rows give to the shapes of support`s store that an in-place check of a copy of it (the first support store to hold its Relational Schema`s rows) refused as fact types whose every row read the other way round: InvoiceHasBillingPeriod, InvoiceHasCostCenter, ProviderResourceHasCostCenter and ServiceHasGitHubRepository, and GitHubRepositoryHasFullName read as <repository, service>. The fixture is Service(.Service Name) with at most one GitHub Repository(.Full Name), a GitHub Repository having no table of its own, and Invoice(.Cost Center, .Billing Period) over Cost Center(.Cost Center Name), itself a component of Invoice Line Item(.Invoice, .Line Item Index). Service`s gitHubRepository column is for ServiceHasGitHubRepository.2 and for a role of GitHub Repository`s reference fact type; Invoice`s costCenter for InvoiceHasCostCenter.2 and CostCenterHasCostCenterName.2; and Invoice Line Item`s key columns unpack Invoice, so they are for InvoiceHasCostCenter.2 and InvoiceHasBillingPeriod.2 as well. Each fact type must be placed in its subject`s table, read by that table`s key: ServiceHasGitHubRepository by serviceName and gitHubRepository, InvoiceHasCostCenter and InvoiceHasBillingPeriod by Invoice`s reference column and the component`s column. Run first, schema:carried gave Service`s gitHubRepository to GitHubRepositoryHasFullName and Invoice`s costCenter to CostCenterHasCostCenterName, the least names, and InvoiceHasBillingPeriod to two columns, so all three were placed nowhere (#) and this answered F.",
DEF("test:csj_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("csj.md"), A("Service Name is a value type.\nFull Name is a value type.\nCost Center Name is a value type.\nBilling Period is a value type.\nLine Item Index is a value type.\nAmount is a value type.\nService(.Service Name) is an entity type.\nGitHub Repository(.Full Name) is an entity type.\nCost Center(.Cost Center Name) is an entity type.\nInvoice(.Cost Center, .Billing Period) is an entity type.\nInvoice Line Item(.Invoice, .Line Item Index) is an entity type.\nService has GitHub Repository.\n  Each Service has at most one GitHub Repository.\nCost Center has Amount.\n  Each Cost Center has at most one Amount.\nInvoice has Cost Center.\nInvoice has Billing Period.\nInvoice Line Item has Invoice.\nInvoice Line Item has Line Item Index.\n"), A("csj/csj.md"))))),
DEF("test:csj_store",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:csj_files"))),
