       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), K(A("\"<refused>\"")))), K(PHI()),
          S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("quote_str"), A("main:case_text"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("case")), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1))))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)))), K(PHI()),
             S2(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1))))))),
"THE ARTIFACT IS ONE MORE RENDER TARGET, AND ITS LAWS COME FIRST (an artifact is like a custom native view, to which arest data may be bound, powered through its own fact base). A claude.ai artifact is a published HTML page, so its widgets are the html: realizations lambda already carries, and its layout engine is render:artifact, the Render Target readings/ui/render-target-instances.md declares, whose body is lambda`s artifact:page: one self-contained document from the panes navigate answers. test:artifact_pairs holds that the pairing covers every control kind the view emits: every kind the placed rows of a fixture entity screen carry, their children and the view`s menu among them, is a declared control, each has its html: realization in the store, and the artifact`s registration, render:<kind> for each declared control with a realization and render:artifact as its engine, leaves ui:unpaired_of nothing. test:artifact_links holds Theorem 2 of the emitted page: the hrefs the page carries, read back out of its text, are the links the entity screen carries, its transitions at its status as ui:transitions answers them over a store with a machine, Support Response r1 at Draft offered approve and redraft, and its nav item, as many as there are and no other. The nav leg is the literal shape ui:facts answers; the transitions leg is computed. Before artifact:page exists both answer F, through test:artifact_built, and not by dying. Operand of both: the composed store, which gives the declared controls; the fixture is literal.",
