"A PLATFORM OPENED AT AN ENTITY SHOWS ITS COLLECTION IN THE MASTER. An artifact page is a platform whose first navigation is the address it was published at, so its stacks are empty and its address is an entity, Issue iss-artifact-200 on pm. The entity went to the detail pane and the master, holding no view, drew the vanity layer, the description of whichever domain the store lists last, which on pm`s copy is a lambda note about induce. iFactr`s master holds the list a detail is chosen from, so a platform that registers more than one pane and is opened at an entity of an addressable type holds that type`s collection in its master and the entity at the detail`s root. test:artifact_master asks it of ui:navp over the composed store: fresh master and detail stacks and the address Function Function leave the master holding the collection Function and the detail the entity. It answered F first, the master left empty.",
DEF("test:artifact_master",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), N(2), A("ui:navp"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(S2(A("master"), PHI()), S2(A("detail"), PHI()))), K(S2(A("Function"), A("Function"))))),
       K(S2(S2(A("master"), S1(S1(A("Function")))), S2(A("detail"), S1(S2(A("Function"), A("Function"))))))))),
"AN ENTITY SCREEN SHOWS THE STATUS ITS MACHINE HOLDS IT AT. An entity of a type with a machine showed its columns, its relations and its transitions, and nowhere the status it stands at: the actions section carried it in its title, which ui:viewprops makes the title of the view`s Menu, and no widget draws a menu`s title, so an Issue at Filed read Filed nowhere on its artifact page. test:artifact_status asks it of the page: the entity screen of the fixture`s Support Response r1, ui:entity_at over test:artifact_store, arranged and written by artifact:page, carries the field ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus with the value Draft. It answered F first.",
