"test:check_sql holds the SQL checks to the in-memory judge (every constraint is one SQL query whose rows are its violating instances). Each fixture is a readings file, the populations of its fact types and its instances` classification, and V when it holds a violation or C when it holds none; the store is the one compile:check makes of the readings with those populations and that classification, and the Constraint rows the reflection answers for it (Constraint is of Constraint Type, its modality, Constraint Span and its numbers, Object Type plays Role). The rows sqlite:check_in answers over a database with no file (sqlite:scratch) that the store`s script lays out and fills (sqlite:store_script), each <fact type, kind, instance> with its constraint dropped, must be the rows ui:violations answers of the store, and those are some for a V fixture and none for a C one. One pair of fixtures for each type check:all says: a uniqueness over one role that is not its table`s primary key (Crate has Tag, one Crate a Tag); a mandatory (Crate has some Weight); a subset (a Crate shipped is checked); and the deontic mandatory, uniqueness and subset, whose rows are the same queries` read as deontic. Run first with check:all answering no entry, it failed.",
