"<V or C, store> to T when the SQL checks answer what the judge answers, and that is some for V and none for C.",
DEF("test:cs_ok",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cs_sql"), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:violations"), N(2)))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("V")))), S5(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), A("ui:violations"), N(2)), S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("ui:violations"), N(2)))))),
DEF("test:cs_one",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cs_ok"), S3(A("CONS"), N(4), A("test:cs_store")))),
DEF("test:check_sql",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:cs_one")), A("test:cs_fx"))),
"test:validate_all holds the validate verb to every alethic violation a store holds at rest. validate answered the uniquenesses alone (cmd:validate over the descriptors), so a store holding a mandatory or a subset violation validated clean. The fixture is one readings file holding one violation of each of three kinds: two Crates with one Tag where For each Tag, at most one Crate has that Tag; a Crate with no Weight where Each Crate has some Weight; and a Crate shipped and not checked where a shipped Crate is checked. validate of the store answers exactly the alethic violations the in-memory judge answers of it, each <fact type, kind, instance>, and they are three, one uniqueness, one mandatory and one subset. Run first with validate answering the uniquenesses alone, it failed.",
DEF("test:va_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cs_store"), K(S4(A("Name is a value type.\nTag is a value type.\nWeight is a value type.\nCrate(.Name) is an entity type.\nCrate has Tag.\n  Each Crate has at most one Tag.\n  For each Tag, at most one Crate has that Tag.\nCrate has Weight.\n  Each Crate has at most one Weight.\n  Each Crate has some Weight.\nCrate is shipped.\nCrate is checked.\nIf some Crate is shipped then that Crate is checked.\n"),
       S3(S2(A("CrateHasTag"), S2(S2(A("c1"), A("t")), S2(A("c2"), A("t")))), S2(A("CrateHasWeight"), S1(S2(A("c1"), A("w")))), S2(A("CrateIsShipped"), S1(S1(A("c2"))))),
       S2(S2(A("c1"), A("Crate")), S2(A("c2"), A("Crate"))), A("V"))))),
