"test:fact_reflect holds the Facts a store reflects to literal rows, and feeds them to an investigation. Sherlock is independent of the facts, and may be fed any fact set to induce the answer to a query. The store holds three asserted facts, Julia Stoner died unexplained, the ventilator connects her bedroom to the study, and Enoch Drebber was poisoned, and the selection fed is the first two fact types. reflect:facts answers each row of the selection as the Fact of instances.md and nothing else: the Fact is of its Fact Type, fills each Role of it, and the RoleInstance of each, the pair spelled as every objectified instance is, uses the value the row holds at that position. A Fact is spelled as an Event is spelled less its time (store:ev_spell), the fact type, a colon, and each position=value joined by a bar. Then the rule of a literal readings fixture of the Sherlock shape, a Case observes an Observation that is of a Fact and proposes a Hypothesis that expects a Fact Type, is read by the reader and evaluated over the case rows and the reflected Facts: the case corroborates the trained snake, whose fact type the fed set holds, and not the gypsies, whose observation is of a fact outside the selection. Run first with reflect:facts answering nothing, it failed (fact-reflect -> F).",
DEF("test:fr_store",
    K(S3(S3(A("CELL"), A("PersonDiedUnexplained"), S1(S1(A("Julia Stoner")))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom"), S1(S3(A("the ventilator"), A("her bedroom"), A("the study")))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("PersonWasPoisoned"), S1(S1(A("Enoch Drebber"))))))),
DEF("test:fr_facts",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("reflect:facts"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("PersonDiedUnexplained"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom"))), A("test:fr_store")))),
DEF("test:fr_text",
    K(S2(A("fr.md"), A("Case(.Name) is an entity type.\nObservation(.Title) is an entity type.\nHypothesis(.Claim) is an entity type.\nFact(.Fact Id) is an entity type.\nFact Type(.Fact Type Name) is an entity type.\nName is a value type.\nTitle is a value type.\nClaim is a value type.\nFact Id is a value type.\nFact Type Name is a value type.\n\nCase observes Observation.\nObservation is of Fact.\nCase proposes Hypothesis.\nFact is of Fact Type.\nHypothesis expects Fact Type.\n\nCase corroborates Hypothesis. *\n\n* Case corroborates Hypothesis iff that Case proposes that Hypothesis and that Case observes some Observation and that Observation is of some Fact and that Fact is of some Fact Type and that Hypothesis expects that Fact Type.\n")))),
DEF("test:fr_case",
    K(S4(
       S2(A("CaseObservesObservation"), S3(S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the unexplained death")), S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the ventilator passage")), S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the poisoning")))),
       S2(A("ObservationIsOfFact"), S3(S2(A("the unexplained death"), A("PersonDiedUnexplained:1=Julia Stoner")), S2(A("the ventilator passage"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom:1=the ventilator|2=her bedroom|3=the study")), S2(A("the poisoning"), A("PersonWasPoisoned:1=Enoch Drebber")))),
       S2(A("CaseProposesHypothesis"), S2(S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("a trained snake killed her")), S2(A("The Speckled Band"), A("the gypsies killed her")))),
       S2(A("HypothesisExpectsFactType"), S2(S2(A("a trained snake killed her"), A("FixtureConnectsRoomToRoom")), S2(A("the gypsies killed her"), A("PersonWasPoisoned"))))))),
