DEF("test:all",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("test:report")))
,
"A NAME DECLARED IN TWO DOMAINS AT ONE LEVEL IS SAID, AND BOTH DOMAINS ARE NAMED. Namespacing is done by domain, not by hacking up the name: domains provide the namespace. core.md declares that each Function belongs to at most one Domain and has at most one Local Name, and that for each Domain and Local Name at most one Function belongs to that Domain and has that Local Name. The reader recorded a file`s Domain only against the types that file declares, read an instance sentence with no file at all, and reflect:fbd_first kept the first Domain of an id and dropped the others without a word. test:local_names reads three files, two at one level and one at another: fx/a.md and fx/b.md each declare Gizmo, under the Domains alpha and beta, and each says that Widget `w1` is labeled; gx/c.md declares Gizmo under gamma. Over what compile:check answers for them, state:localnames holds <name, Domain, noun, level> for each of the three declarations of Gizmo and for the instance w1 in each file at fx/; the findings name exactly one collision, Gizmo, and its Domains are alpha and beta -- w1 is one Widget spoken of in two files, and gamma is at another level, which the cascade resolves; and the arm reflect:arms gives FunctionHasLocalName answers <Gizmo, Gizmo> over those cells. Before the reader records any of it, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:ln_files",
    K(S3(S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget is labeled.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("fx/a.md")),
         S3(A("b.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nDomain 'beta' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("fx/b.md")),
         S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("gx/c.md"))))),
"<name, text, path>: the file`s pair as compile:file_pair makes it from the file it reads.",
DEF("test:ln_pair",
    S3(A("COMP"), S6(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:domain_fault"), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)))), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:pair_of_rows"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:text_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2)))), N(3)))),
"<cells, findings> of test:ln_files, as compile:check answers them for files it reads.",
DEF("test:ln_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:ln_files")))),
