DEF("test:ln_arm",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FunctionHasLocalName")), A("reflect:arms")))),
DEF("test:ln_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))), N(1))),
DEF("test:local_names",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S9(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("Gizmo"), A("alpha"), A("Object Type"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("Gizmo"), A("beta"), A("Object Type"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("Gizmo"), A("gamma"), A("Object Type"), A("gx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("w1"), A("alpha"), A("Widget"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("w1"), A("beta"), A("Widget"), A("fx/"))), A("test:ln_rows"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("test:ln_coll")), K(S1(A("Gizmo"))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:ln_coll")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), N(4), N(1), A("test:ln_coll")), K(S2(A("alpha"), A("beta")))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:ln_arm")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Gizmo"), A("Gizmo"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("apply"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:ln_arm"), A("test:ln_store"))))))),
       A("test:ln_run")))),
"<store>: the composed store with LawPrSrc, a Thing with a Basis, asserted; LawPrOwn and LawPrFed, a Thing with a Value, each marked + and derived as the projection of LawPrSrc, unique on the Thing; and LawPrFed federated at the JSON Path law-pr-value.",
DEF("test:pr_schema",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
                K(S2(A("state:fts"), S3(
                   S5(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawPrOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawPrFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI())))))),
             K(S2(A("state:declared"), S3(
                S2(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis"))),
                S2(A("LawPrOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value"))),
                S2(A("LawPrFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")))))))),
          K(S2(A("state:derived"), S2(S2(A("LawPrOwn"), A("semi")), S2(A("LawPrFed"), A("semi"))))))),
       K(S2(A("state:rules"), S2(
          S3(A("LawPrOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawPrSrc"), S2(N(1), N(2)))),
          S3(A("LawPrFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawPrSrc"), S2(N(1), N(2)))))))))),
"The asserted rows of the fixture, each <fact type, row>: law-pr-k1 with the Basis law-pr-b1, law-pr-k2 with law-pr-b2, and LawPrFed federated at law-pr-value.",
DEF("test:pr_rows",
    K(S3(
       S2(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-b1"))),
       S2(A("LawPrSrc"), S2(A("law-pr-k2"), A("law-pr-b2"))),
       S2(A("FactTypeIsFederatedAtJSONPath"), S2(A("LawPrFed"), A("law-pr-value")))))),
"<store>: the fixture, its rows put over its schema and closed from it as a write closes, so the rules give LawPrOwn and LawPrFed law-pr-b1 for law-pr-k1 and law-pr-b2 for law-pr-k2.",
DEF("test:pr_fx",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("store:closed_from"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("INSERT"), A("test:dft_put")), A("apndr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("reverse"), A("test:pr_rows")), A("id"))))),
       A("test:pr_schema"))),
"<name, store> to the rows the store holds of the fact type, not the rows a read of it answers: its top-level cell, else its descriptor`s (derive:raw_rows), and its cell in FILE.",
DEF("test:pr_stored",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), A("derive:raw_rows"),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(2)))), K(A("#")))), K(PHI()),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:unnest"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:file_of"), N(2))))))))),
"<store> to the store a fact POST of law-pr-e1 for law-pr-k1 in LawPrOwn leaves over the fixture.",
DEF("test:pr_entered",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pr_fx"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1")))))),
"<store> to the store a fact DELETE of that entered row leaves after it.",
DEF("test:pr_retracted",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:retract_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pr_entered"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1")))))),
"<store> to the store after a fact POST of law-pr-e1 for law-pr-k1 in LawPrFed as well.",
DEF("test:pr_both",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pr_entered"), K(A("LawPrFed")), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1")))))),
"The facts a page of a sync reads: law-pr-s1 for law-pr-k1 in LawPrFed, which is federated, and in LawPrOwn, which is not.",
DEF("test:pr_page",
    K(S2(S3(A("LawPrFed"), A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-s1")), S3(A("LawPrOwn"), A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-s1"))))),
"<store> to the store a sync of that page leaves over test:pr_both (fed:sync_write).",
DEF("test:pr_synced",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("fed:sync_write"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:pr_both"), A("test:pr_page")))),
"AN ENTERED VALUE OVERRIDES THE DERIVED ONE FOR ITS KEY, AND ONLY WHAT WAS ENTERED IS STORED. Halpin and Morgan 2008, pp. 100-101: `*` is derived on query, `**` derived and stored, `+` semi-derived. An entered + row isn`t beside a derived row, it overrides it, and a value entered is not overwritten. A + head is read as a `*` head is, computed when it is read, and what it stores is what was entered. Over test:pr_fx, after a fact POST of law-pr-e1 for law-pr-k1 in LawPrOwn: a read of LawPrOwn answers law-pr-e1 for law-pr-k1, the entered value, and law-pr-b2 for law-pr-k2, the derived one, and nothing else; and the store holds the entered row and neither row the rule derives, law-pr-b2 for law-pr-k2 nor law-pr-b1 for law-pr-k1. A store holding the derived row of law-pr-k2 beside the entered one, the closure merging the two into the cell, is what this law refuses.",
DEF("test:plus_entered",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1")), S2(A("law-pr-k2"), A("law-pr-b2")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k2"), A("law-pr-b2"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pr_entered")))),
"A RETRACT OF THE ENTERED VALUE RESTORES THE DERIVED DEFAULT, AND STORES NOTHING OF IT. A field with a default uses the default after retract. Over test:pr_entered, after a fact DELETE of law-pr-e1 for law-pr-k1 in LawPrOwn: a read of LawPrOwn answers law-pr-b1 for law-pr-k1 and law-pr-b2 for law-pr-k2, the rule`s values, and nothing else; and the store holds none of the three rows, the entered one gone and the derived ones never kept. A store holding both derived rows is what this law refuses.",
DEF("test:plus_retracted",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-b1")), S2(A("law-pr-k2"), A("law-pr-b2")))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k2"), A("law-pr-b2"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pr_retracted")))),
"A SYNC REPLACES AN ENTERED VALUE OF A FEDERATED + FACT TYPE, AND NOTHING DERIVED REPLACES ONE THE USER OWNS. A sync from an external federation is a derivation; for a federated fact type an entered value is a write-through to the system and the next sync replaces it (the data is updated if someone else changed it); for one the user owns, not federated, an entered value is never overwritten. A fact type is federated where the store declares it federated at a JSON Path or a Function yields it. Over test:pr_both, where law-pr-e1 is entered for law-pr-k1 in LawPrFed, federated, and in LawPrOwn, not, a sync of a page that reads law-pr-s1 for law-pr-k1 in both: the store no longer holds the entered row of LawPrFed, and a read screen shows the page`s fact for it (fed:shown_fact), a + fact type being read through and not cached; while LawPrOwn still answers law-pr-e1 for law-pr-k1, and neither the rule`s law-pr-b1 nor the page`s law-pr-s1. The federated half fails where the sync writes nothing of a + fact type, so the entered row stays and wins on the screen.",
DEF("test:plus_federated",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S6(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrFed")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("fed:shown_fact"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("LawPrFed"), A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-s1"))), A("id"))), K(S3(A("LawPrFed"), A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-s1"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pr-k1"), A("law-pr-s1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPrOwn")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pr_synced")))),
"<store>: the composed store with LawPpSrc, a Thing with a Basis, asserted; LawPpOwn and LawPpFed, a Thing with a Value, each marked ++ and derived as the projection of LawPpSrc, unique on the Thing; and LawPpFed federated at the JSON Path law-pp-value.",
DEF("test:pp_schema",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
                K(S2(A("state:fts"), S3(
                   S5(A("LawPpSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawPpOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawPpFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI())))))),
             K(S2(A("state:declared"), S3(
                S2(A("LawPpSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis"))),
                S2(A("LawPpOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value"))),
                S2(A("LawPpFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")))))))),
          K(S2(A("state:derived"), S2(S2(A("LawPpOwn"), A("semi-derived-and-stored")), S2(A("LawPpFed"), A("semi-derived-and-stored"))))))),
       K(S2(A("state:rules"), S2(
          S3(A("LawPpOwn"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawPpSrc"), S2(N(1), N(2)))),
          S3(A("LawPpFed"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawPpSrc"), S2(N(1), N(2)))))))))),
"The asserted rows of the ++ fixture, each <fact type, row>: law-pp-k1 with the Basis law-pp-b1, law-pp-k2 with law-pp-b2, and LawPpFed federated at law-pp-value.",
DEF("test:pp_rows",
    K(S3(
       S2(A("LawPpSrc"), S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-b1"))),
       S2(A("LawPpSrc"), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2"))),
       S2(A("FactTypeIsFederatedAtJSONPath"), S2(A("LawPpFed"), A("law-pp-value")))))),
"<store>: the ++ fixture, its rows put over its schema and closed from it as a write closes, so the rules give LawPpOwn and LawPpFed law-pp-b1 for law-pp-k1 and law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2, stored, and the record of derived rows holds both.",
DEF("test:pp_fx",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("store:closed_from"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("INSERT"), A("test:dft_put")), A("apndr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("reverse"), A("test:pp_rows")), A("id"))))),
       A("test:pp_schema"))),
"<name, store> to the rows the record of derived rows (derive:rec, state:derived_rows) holds of the fact type: the rows of it a closure derived, as against those entered.",
DEF("test:pp_rec",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:pop"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:rec"), N(2))))),
"<store> to the store a fact POST of law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpOwn leaves over the ++ fixture.",
DEF("test:pp_entered",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pp_fx"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1")))))),
"<store> to the store a fact DELETE of law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2 in LawPpSrc, an input of the rule, leaves after test:pp_entered.",
DEF("test:pp_less",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:retract_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pp_entered"), K(A("LawPpSrc")), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2")))))),
"<store> to the store a fact POST of law-pp-b3 for law-pp-k2 in LawPpSrc leaves after that: the input of law-pp-k2 moved from law-pp-b2 to law-pp-b3.",
DEF("test:pp_moved",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pp_less"), K(A("LawPpSrc")), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b3")))))),
"<store> to the store a fact DELETE of the entered row, law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpOwn, leaves after test:pp_entered.",
DEF("test:pp_retracted",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:retract_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pp_entered"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1")))))),
"<store> to the store after a fact POST of law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpFed as well.",
DEF("test:pp_both",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:pp_entered"), K(A("LawPpFed")), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1")))))),
"The facts a page of a sync reads: law-pp-s1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpFed, which is federated, and in LawPpOwn, which is not.",
DEF("test:pp_page",
    K(S2(S3(A("LawPpFed"), A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-s1")), S3(A("LawPpOwn"), A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-s1"))))),
"<store> to the store a sync of that page leaves over test:pp_both (fed:sync_write).",
DEF("test:pp_synced",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("fed:sync_write"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:pp_both"), A("test:pp_page")))),
"A ++ HEAD IS STORED AND MAINTAINED, AND AN ENTERED VALUE OVERRIDES THE DERIVED ONE FOR ITS KEY. Halpin and Morgan 2008, pp. 100-101: ++ is semi-derived and stored. A ++ head stores derivation and updates, and accepts overrides; a value entered is not overwritten. The store tells an entered row of a ++ head from a derived one by the record of derived rows, state:derived_rows (derive:rec): a write records, for each head it changed that the rule does not own, the rows it holds less those the store asserts, and a closure seeds the head with its rows less that record, so an entered row owns its key (derive:sm_one) and a derived row is the rule`s to take back. Over test:pp_fx, after a fact POST of law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpOwn: a read answers law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 and law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2 and nothing else; the store holds both rows, the derived one maintained beside the entered one; and the record holds law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2 as derived and not the entered row.",
DEF("test:plusplus_entered",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S7(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1")), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pp_rec"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pp_rec"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pp_entered")))),
"AN INPUT THAT MOVES RE-DERIVES WHAT WAS DERIVED, AND LEAVES WHAT WAS ENTERED. A ++ head stores derivation and updates, and accepts overrides. Over test:pp_entered, after the Basis of law-pp-k2 in LawPpSrc moves from law-pp-b2 to law-pp-b3 (a fact DELETE, then a fact POST): a read of LawPpOwn answers law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1, still the entered value, and law-pp-b3 for law-pp-k2, derived again, and nothing else; the store holds law-pp-b3 for law-pp-k2, maintained; and the record holds it as derived and not the entered row. A write resets a head the record holds derived rows of to what the store asserts of it when an input lost rows, and its rules derive the rest again.",
DEF("test:plusplus_maintained",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1")), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b3")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b3"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b3"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pp_rec"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pp_rec"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pp_moved")))),
"A RETRACT OF THE ENTERED VALUE OF A ++ HEAD SHOWS THE DERIVED VALUE AGAIN, STORED. A field with a default uses the default after retract. Over test:pp_entered, after a fact DELETE of law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpOwn: a read answers law-pp-b1 for law-pp-k1 and law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2, the rule`s values, and nothing else; the store holds law-pp-b1 for law-pp-k1 again, derived when the entered row went; and the record holds it as derived. The head lost a row of its own, so its rules read everything and law-pp-b1 comes back.",
DEF("test:plusplus_retracted",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-b1")), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pr_stored"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pp_rec"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pp_retracted")))),
"A SYNC REPLACES AN ENTERED VALUE OF A FEDERATED ++ FACT TYPE, AND NOTHING DERIVED REPLACES ONE THE USER OWNS. A sync from an external federation is a derivation; for a federated fact type the next sync replaces an entered value (the data is updated if someone else changed it); for one the user owns, nothing derived ever overwrites an entered value. Over test:pp_both, where law-pp-e1 is entered for law-pp-k1 in LawPpFed, federated, and in LawPpOwn, not, a sync of a page that reads law-pp-s1 for law-pp-k1 in both: a read of LawPpFed answers the page`s law-pp-s1 for law-pp-k1 and not the entered law-pp-e1, and still law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2, which the page does not name; while LawPpOwn still answers law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1, and neither the page`s law-pp-s1 nor the rule`s law-pp-b1. The federated half fails where a page drops a fact of a ++ fact type whose key the store holds a row for (fed:held_key), so the entered row stays and wins.",
DEF("test:plusplus_federated",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S7(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-s1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpFed")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpFed")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpFed")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-s1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id"))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pp_synced")))),
"<store> to <the ++ fixture, the store a fact POST of law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpOwn leaves over it>, the fixture closed once.",
DEF("test:rd_one",
    S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawPpOwn")), K(S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1")))))), A("test:pp_fx"))),
"<store> to <the ++ fixture, the store after the entering write, the store a fact PUT of law-pp-b3 for law-pp-k2 in LawPpSrc leaves over that>: the PUT is one write that moves the input of law-pp-k2 from law-pp-b2 to law-pp-b3.",
DEF("test:rd_chain",
    S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:replace_step"), S4(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("LawPpSrc")), K(S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b3")))))), A("test:rd_one"))),
"<store> to <the record delta of the entering write, the record delta of the PUT, the ledger rows of the PUT> (derive:rec_delta, derive:rec_ledger).",
DEF("test:rd_deltas",
    S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:rec_delta"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2))), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:rec_delta"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), N(3))), S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:rec_ledger"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), N(3)))), A("test:rd_chain"))),
"A WRITE ANSWERS WHAT IT CHANGED OF THE RECORD OF DERIVED ROWS, AND THE STORE KEEPS IT. A ++ head stores derivation and updates, and accepts overrides; a value entered is not overwritten. So the entered or derived standing of a stored row of a ++ head must outlive a restart. The record of derived rows (state:derived_rows, derive:rec) was seeded at a start from the compile ledger _derived alone, and a row a write derived was recorded in memory only: after a restart it read as entered, an input change no longer derived it again, and it owned its key. derive:rec_delta answers the record delta of a write, the pairs <head, row> it gained and lost, and derive:rec_ledger the same as _derived rows, which the write-back keeps in the transaction that stores the populations. Over test:pp_fx: the fact POST of law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpOwn adds nothing to the record and takes law-pp-b1 for law-pp-k1 in LawPpOwn out of it, the entered value now owning the key; then a fact PUT of law-pp-b3 for law-pp-k2 in LawPpSrc, one write, adds law-pp-b3 for law-pp-k2 in LawPpOwn and LawPpFed and takes law-pp-b2 for law-pp-k2 out of both, and nothing else; its ledger rows carry the row text as the compile writes it; and the entered law-pp-e1 for law-pp-k1 appears in neither delta. It fails where derive:rec_delta answers the empty delta. Expected T once derive:rec_delta takes the record before less the record after and the converse, head by head.",
DEF("test:plusplus_record",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S8(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), N(1), N(1)),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), K(S1(S2(A("LawPpOwn"), S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-b1"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), K(S2(S2(A("LawPpOwn"), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b3"))), S2(A("LawPpFed"), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b3"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)), K(S2(S2(A("LawPpOwn"), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2"))), S2(A("LawPpFed"), S2(A("law-pp-k2"), A("law-pp-b2"))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("LawPpOwn"), A("[\"law-pp-k2\",\"law-pp-b3\"]"))), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(3)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("LawPpOwn"), A("[\"law-pp-k2\",\"law-pp-b2\"]"))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(3)))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("LawPpOwn"), S2(A("law-pp-k1"), A("law-pp-e1")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), N(2))))))),
       A("test:rd_deltas")))),
"<store>: the composed store with LawOgSrc, a Thing with a Basis, asserted; LawOgPlus, a Thing with a Value, marked + and derived as the projection of LawOgSrc; and LawOgStar, a Thing with a Value, marked * and derived as the projection of LawOgPlus; each unique on the Thing. No head the store keeps reads either, so the store computes both on read.",
DEF("test:og_schema",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
                K(S2(A("state:fts"), S3(
                   S5(A("LawOgSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawOgPlus"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI()),
                   S5(A("LawOgStar"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), PHI())))))),
             K(S2(A("state:declared"), S3(
                S2(A("LawOgSrc"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Basis"))),
                S2(A("LawOgPlus"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value"))),
                S2(A("LawOgStar"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")))))))),
          K(S2(A("state:derived"), S2(S2(A("LawOgPlus"), A("semi")), S2(A("LawOgStar"), A("full"))))))),
       K(S2(A("state:rules"), S2(
          S3(A("LawOgPlus"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawOgSrc"), S2(N(1), N(2)))),
          S3(A("LawOgStar"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Value")), S3(A("proj"), A("LawOgPlus"), S2(N(1), N(2)))))))))),
"The asserted rows of the on-read guard fixture, each <fact type, row>: law-og-k1 with the Basis law-og-b1, law-og-k2 with law-og-b2.",
DEF("test:og_rows",
    K(S2(
       S2(A("LawOgSrc"), S2(A("law-og-k1"), A("law-og-b1"))),
       S2(A("LawOgSrc"), S2(A("law-og-k2"), A("law-og-b2")))))),
"<store> to the fixture, its rows put over its schema and closed from it as a write closes, then a fact POST of law-og-e1 for law-og-k1 in LawOgPlus.",
DEF("test:og_entered",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("store:closed_from"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("INSERT"), A("test:dft_put")), A("apndr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("reverse"), A("test:og_rows")), A("id"))))),
          A("test:og_schema")),
       K(A("LawOgPlus")), K(S2(A("law-og-k1"), A("law-og-e1")))))),
"A RULE THAT READS A + HEAD ON READ SEES THE ENTERED VALUE, NOT THE DERIVED ONE (for a + head, an entered value overrides the derived one). A read computes a `*` head and the + heads its rules read in one cone (derive:on_read), the + heads seeded with what was entered (derive:or_seeds). The cone`s fixpoint takes its rules guarded as a closure takes them (derive:or_fix over derive:guarded), so the + head`s rule drops the row it derives for a key a value is entered for, and the `*` head never reads it. Over test:og_entered, where both heads are computed on read and law-og-e1 is entered for law-og-k1 in LawOgPlus: a read of LawOgStar answers law-og-e1 for law-og-k1 and law-og-b2 for law-og-k2 and nothing else, so not the derived law-og-b1; and a read of LawOgPlus answers the same. With derive:or_fix bypassed (derive over the unguarded rules), LawOgStar`s rule read law-og-b1 beside law-og-e1 for law-og-k1, the functional filter of a `*` head (derive:sm_full) dropped a key given two values, and a read of LawOgStar answered law-og-b2 for law-og-k2 alone, so the entered value was lost to the `*` head; this answered F.",
DEF("test:plus_read_guard",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S6(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawOgStar")), A("derive:or_heads"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawOgPlus")), A("derive:or_heads"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawOgStar")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("law-og-k1"), A("law-og-e1")), S2(A("law-og-k2"), A("law-og-b2")))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("law-og-k1"), A("law-og-b1"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawOgStar")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawOgPlus")), A("id"))), K(S2(S2(A("law-og-k1"), A("law-og-e1")), S2(A("law-og-k2"), A("law-og-b2"))))))),
       A("test:og_entered")))),

"EVERY TABLE THE MAP NAMES HAS A KEY. federation.md declares `Response is an entity type.` with no reference mode and no supertype, so the map gave it a table of its own and no primary key, rmap:keyed dropped it from rmap:coltabs, and rmap:unkeyed named it where no host prints it; the DDL never created Response and the write-back inserted into it. Every other entity type of the metamodel identifies through Function(.id), by a reference mode or by a declared subtyping. Over the composed base store rmap:unkeyed answers nothing. Before the map gave Response an identity it answered <Response, Response>, and this answered F.",
DEF("test:unkeyed_none",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("rmap:unkeyed"))),

"test:tab_facts answers the fact types the columns of one table walk: operand <table, rmap:ctab>, each entry <concept, table, columns>, each column <owner, flag, path>, each step of a path carrying its fact types at 5, the empty list for an assimilation step.",
DEF("test:tab_facts",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"),
       S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"),
          S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"),
             S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("lt"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), A("id")), K(N(5)))), K(PHI()), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("atom"), N(5)), K(PHI()), N(5)))),
             N(3))),
          N(3))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"),
          S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)), N(1))), S2(A("CONS"), N(2)), K(PHI()))),
          A("distl")))),

"A RESPONSE IS AN OBJECT TYPE INSTANCE, SO ITS FACTS LAND WHERE A FAILURE`S DO. No reading says `Response is a subtype of Object Type Instance.`: all objects are object type instances. An entity type with no identification of its own identifies as every object does, through Function(.id), its instances Object Type Instances, so the map absorbs it as it absorbs a declared subtype of Object Type Instance (Failure, outcomes.md). Over the composed base store: Function is a keyed table, no table is named Response, and the four fact types federation.md declares for Response -- answers Function, is from Url, has HTTP Status Code, occurred at Timestamp -- are walked by columns of the Function table. Before the map gave Response an identity, Response was a table of its own, and this answered F.",
DEF("test:response_keyed",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Function")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("rmap:pkrows")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Response")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("rmap:ctab"))))),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), A("distr"),
          S3(A("CONS"),
             K(S4(A("ResponseAnswersFunction"), A("ResponseIsFromUrl"), A("ResponseHasHTTPStatusCode"), A("ResponseOccurredAtTimestamp"))),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("test:tab_facts"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Function")), A("rmap:ctab")))))))),

"A WRITE-BACK NAMES ONLY TABLES THE DDL CREATED. Two checks. Over a literal map of two tables, Kept with a primary key and Dropped with none, the tables the write-back walks are Kept alone: a table without a key is one rmap:coltabs leaves out and the DDL never creates, so the write-back may not name it either. And over the composed base store every table rmap:writeback walks is one rmap:coltabs creates. While rmap:writeback was rmap:ctab, the walk host.js emitToDb made, the first answered Kept and Dropped, the second named Response, and this answered F. Since a view head is not in rmap:coltabs, rmap:writeback reads rmap:coltabs as well, so the literal map holds a kept rmap:coltabs; it names Dropped too, so the key gate is still what leaves Dropped out.",
DEF("test:writeback_keyed",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:writeback"),
             K(S3(S3(A("CELL"), A("stored:rmap:ctab"), S2(S3(A("Kept"), A("Kept"), PHI()), S3(A("Dropped"), A("Dropped"), PHI()))),
                  S3(A("CELL"), A("stored:rmap:pkrows"), S1(S4(A("pk"), A("Kept"), PHI(), A("Kept_PK")))),
                  S3(A("CELL"), A("stored:rmap:coltabs"), S2(S2(A("Kept"), PHI()), S2(A("Dropped"), PHI()))))))),
          K(S1(A("Kept"))))),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("theta:member")), A("distr"),
          S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("rmap:writeback")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("rmap:coltabs"))))))),

"THE COMPOUND FIXTURE: one file declaring Thing(.Aisle, .Bay), Aisle and Color value types, Bay declared nowhere, and Thing has at most one Color. test:ck_run is <cells, findings> as compile:check answers them for it, test:ck_store its cells as a store.",
DEF("test:ck_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("t.md"), A("Aisle is a value type.\nColor is a value type.\nThing(.Aisle, .Bay) is an entity type.\nThing has Color.\n  Each Thing has at most one Color.\n"), A("cx/t.md"))))),
DEF("test:ck_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:ck_files")))),
DEF("test:ck_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ln_store"), A("test:ck_run"))),

"THE COMPOUND SCHEMES ARE READ ONCE PER STATE. read:state_mapinputs maps read:mi_row over every record, so whatever read:mi_row reaches runs once per record, and read:compounds there scanned the whole parse 1,256 times on claude. Lambda cannot count calls, but it can ask its own graph where a name is reached from, as test:unreach_ok does: this law holds when read:compounds and read:cmp_plans_c are reached from read:state_mapinputs, through read:cmp_ctx, and from nothing read:mi_row reaches. test:co_reach walks the definitions a name references, from the names given, to the fixed point. Before read:cmp_ctx, read:mi_row reached read:compounds through read:cmp_near, and this answered F.",
"test:co_refs: <<D, names>, name> to the names the definition of name references.",
DEF("test:co_refs",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:refs_of"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1))))),
"test:co_new: <D, names, seen, frontier> to the names the frontier references that are not yet seen.",
DEF("test:co_new",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("theta:dedup"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:co_refs")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distl"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2)), N(4)))),
       N(3)))),
DEF("test:co_step",
    S3(A("COMP"), S5(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)), N(2))), N(2)),
       S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:co_new")))),
"test:co_reach: <D, names> to every name reached from them, themselves included.",
DEF("test:co_reach",
    S4(A("COMP"), N(3), S3(A("WHILE"), S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), N(4)), A("test:co_step")),
       S5(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:reach_names"), N(1)), N(2), N(2)))),
DEF("test:compounds_once",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("read:compounds")), N(1))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("read:cmp_plans_c")), N(1))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("read:compounds")), N(2))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("read:cmp_plans_c")), N(2))))),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:co_reach"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S1(A("read:mi_row"))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:co_reach"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S1(A("read:state_mapinputs")))))))),

"A COMPOUND REFERENCE SCHEME IS THE PREFERRED IDENTIFIER, AND THE MAP KEYS ITS TABLE BY IT. Compound ids have to work. Halpin 3.6 and ch. 10: `Thing(.Aisle, .Bay)` declares a fact type per component, Thing has Aisle and Thing has Bay, each functional and mandatory for Thing, and an external uniqueness over the component roles that is Thing`s preferred identifier; the map makes that uniqueness the table`s primary key. A reader that reads the parenthesized list as no reference mode records nothing, so the entity has no identification at all, its table no key, and rmap:unkeyed names it. Over test:ck_store: state:ucs carries the preferred external uniqueness UC:ep:ThingHasAisle#2+ThingHasBay#2, and rmap:pkrows keys the Thing table on two columns. Before the reader carried the list, neither held, and this answered F.",
DEF("test:compound_keyed",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("UC:ep:ThingHasAisle#2+ThingHasBay#2")),
          S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("theta:flatten"),
             S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("T")))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI()))), A("rmap:ucrows"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Thing")))), S2(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), N(4))), K(PHI()))), A("rmap:pkrows"))),
          K(S1(N(2)))))),
       A("test:ck_store")))),

"Two Things, t1 and t2, under the preferred external uniqueness of Thing(.Aisle, .Bay): both in Aisle a1, and in Bay b1 (test:cu_dup) or t2 in Bay b2 (test:cu_ok).",
DEF("test:cu_dup",
    K(S4(S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("ThingHasAisle"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("t1"), S1(A("a1"))), S3(A("CELL"), A("t2"), S1(A("a1"))))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ThingHasBay"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("t1"), S1(A("b1"))), S3(A("CELL"), A("t2"), S1(A("b1"))))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:fts"), S1(S2(S5(A("ThingHasAisle"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Aisle")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("a1")), S2(A("t2"), A("a1")))), S5(A("ThingHasBay"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Bay")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("b1")), S2(A("t2"), A("b1"))))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("Thing")), S2(A("t2"), A("Thing")))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:ucs"), S1(S1(S4(A("UC:ep:ThingHasAisle#2+ThingHasBay#2"), A("T"), A("F"), S2(S2(A("ThingHasAisle"), N(2)), S2(A("ThingHasBay"), N(2)))))))))),
DEF("test:cu_ok",
    K(S4(S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("ThingHasAisle"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("t1"), S1(A("a1"))), S3(A("CELL"), A("t2"), S1(A("a1"))))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ThingHasBay"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("t1"), S1(A("b1"))), S3(A("CELL"), A("t2"), S1(A("b2"))))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:fts"), S1(S2(S5(A("ThingHasAisle"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Aisle")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("a1")), S2(A("t2"), A("a1")))), S5(A("ThingHasBay"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Bay")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("b1")), S2(A("t2"), A("b2"))))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S2(S2(A("t1"), A("Thing")), S2(A("t2"), A("Thing")))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:ucs"), S1(S1(S4(A("UC:ep:ThingHasAisle#2+ThingHasBay#2"), A("T"), A("F"), S2(S2(A("ThingHasAisle"), N(2)), S2(A("ThingHasBay"), N(2)))))))))),

"TWO THINGS WITH ONE AISLE AND ONE BAY ARE ONE IDENTIFIER TWICE, AND THE WRITE IS REFUSED. A preferred external uniqueness is alethic: no two instances of the entity agree on every component. Over test:cu_dup the uniqueness arm names t1 and t2, its rows are alethic, so the commit gate (Thm 1) refuses; over test:cu_ok, where t2 is in another Bay, it names nothing. Before an arm checked an external uniqueness, cmd:xuc_viols answered nothing for either and this answered F.",
DEF("test:compound_refused",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(3))), A("cmd:xuc_viols"), A("test:cu_dup")), K(S2(A("t1"), A("t2"))))),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), A("main:alethic_of"), S3(A("COMP"), A("cmd:xuc_viols"), A("test:cu_dup"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("cmd:xuc_viols"), A("test:cu_ok"))))),

"THE SCHEME REUSE FIXTURES: Crate identified by Crate(.Shelf, .Slot), Shelf and Slot value types. test:sr_reuse_files also declares `Crate belongs to Shelf.`, test:sr_mint_files declares no binary between Crate and Shelf, and test:sr_ambig_files declares two, `Crate belongs to Shelf.` and `Crate is stored on Shelf.` test:sr_run is <cells, findings> as compile:check answers them for the files, and test:sr_store its cells as a store.",
DEF("test:sr_reuse_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("s.md"), A("Slot is a value type.\nShelf is a value type.\nCrate(.Shelf, .Slot) is an entity type.\nCrate belongs to Shelf.\n"), A("sx/s.md"))))),
DEF("test:sr_mint_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("s.md"), A("Slot is a value type.\nShelf is a value type.\nCrate(.Shelf, .Slot) is an entity type.\n"), A("sx/s.md"))))),
DEF("test:sr_ambig_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("s.md"), A("Slot is a value type.\nShelf is a value type.\nCrate(.Shelf, .Slot) is an entity type.\nCrate belongs to Shelf.\nCrate is stored on Shelf.\n"), A("sx/s.md"))))),
DEF("test:sr_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")))),
DEF("test:sr_store",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ln_store"), A("test:sr_run"))),
"test:sr_stated: the fact types a Crate states when it belongs to its Shelf and has its Slot. The cells compile:of_x answers are not a carrier -- state:declared is whole, not chunked -- so mcp:tools, and with it cmd:mand_viols, cannot be asked of them; the law asks the schema instead: every fact type carrying a mandatory is one of these, so such a Crate violates none.",
DEF("test:sr_stated",
    K(S2(A("CrateBelongsToShelf"), A("CrateHasSlot")))),
"store to the names of its fact types that carry a mandatory.",
DEF("test:sr_mandatory",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"),
       S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), N(4)), K(PHI()), S2(A("CONS"), N(1)))),
       A("store:fts"))),
"store to the names of the fact types whose players are Crate and Shelf, in either order.",
DEF("test:sr_between",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"),
       S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(S2(A("Crate"), A("Shelf"))))), S2(A("CONS"), N(1)), K(PHI()))),
       A("store:fts"))),
"store to the names of its preferred uniquenesses.",
DEF("test:sr_pref",
    S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("theta:flatten"),
       S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("T")))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI()))), A("rmap:ucrows")))),
"findings to whether one of them says the scheme of Crate is ambiguous and names both declared fact types as its candidates.",
DEF("test:sr_ambig_said",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"),
          S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), A("atom"), K(PHI()),
             S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("ambiguous")))),
                S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Crate")))),
                   S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(4), K(S2(A("CrateBelongsToShelf"), A("CrateIsStoredOnShelf"))))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI())),
                   K(PHI())),
                K(PHI()))))))),
"A COMPOUND REFERENCE SCHEME USES THE FACT TYPE THE READINGS DECLARE, AND MINTS ONE ONLY WHERE THEY DECLARE NONE. Halpin: the roles of a reference scheme are the roles of the existing fact types. Measured on support: `Cost Tier(.Variable Cost Source, .Tier Name) is an entity type.` beside the declared `Cost Tier belongs to Variable Cost Source.` gave CostTierBelongsToVariableCostSource and a minted CostTierHasVariableCostSource, mandatory and empty, so all seven Cost Tiers violated it although each states that it belongs to its Variable Cost Source. Over test:sr_reuse_files exactly one fact type joins Crate and Shelf, CrateBelongsToShelf; the preferred external uniqueness is UC:ep:CrateBelongsToShelf#2+CrateHasSlot#2; CrateBelongsToShelf carries the mandatory; and every fact type carrying a mandatory is one test:sr_stated names, so a Crate that belongs to its Shelf and has its Slot violates none. Over test:sr_mint_files, with no binary declared, CrateHasShelf is still minted and the preferred uniqueness is UC:ep:CrateHasShelf#2+CrateHasSlot#2, as compound-keyed pins for Thing. Over test:sr_ambig_files the scheme could use either of two declared fact types, so the findings name both under the kind ambiguous and nothing is minted. While the reader minted Crate has Shelf beside the declared fact type, two fact types joined Crate and Shelf and this answered F.",
DEF("test:scheme_reuse",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_holds"),
       S4(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_store"), A("test:sr_reuse_files")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_store"), A("test:sr_mint_files")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_run"), A("test:sr_ambig_files"))))),
"<reuse store, mint store, ambiguous run>: the checks of test:scheme_reuse, the rest asked only once one fact type joins Crate and Shelf.",
DEF("test:sr_holds",
    S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_between"), N(1)), K(S1(A("CrateBelongsToShelf"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S8(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("UC:ep:CrateBelongsToShelf#2+CrateHasSlot#2")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_pref"), N(1)))),
          S5(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), A("theta:flatten"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("CrateBelongsToShelf")))), S2(A("CONS"), N(4)), K(PHI()))), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:fts"), N(1)))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:subset"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_mandatory"), N(1)), A("test:sr_stated"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("CrateHasShelf")), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("store:fts"), N(2)))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("UC:ep:CrateHasShelf#2+CrateHasSlot#2")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_pref"), N(2)))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_ambig_said"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(3))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("CrateHasShelf")), S5(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("store:fts"), A("test:ln_store"), N(3)))))),
       K(A("F")))),
"A store known clean (state:alethic_clean T) under the preferred external uniqueness of Crate(.Shelf, .Slot): Crate c1 on Shelf s1 in Slot x1, and Crate c2 on Shelf s1 with no Slot yet. Neither component is mandatory, so the store holds no alethic violation.",
DEF("test:xt_fx",
    K(S6(S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("CrateHasShelf"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("c1"), S1(A("s1"))), S3(A("CELL"), A("c2"), S1(A("s1"))))), S3(A("CELL"), A("CrateHasSlot"), S1(S3(A("CELL"), A("c1"), S1(A("x1"))))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:fts"), S1(S2(S5(A("CrateHasShelf"), S2(A("Crate"), A("Shelf")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S2(S2(A("c1"), A("s1")), S2(A("c2"), A("s1")))), S5(A("CrateHasSlot"), S2(A("Crate"), A("Slot")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S1(S2(A("c1"), A("x1"))))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S2(S2(A("c1"), A("Crate")), S2(A("c2"), A("Crate")))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:declared"), S1(S2(S2(A("CrateHasShelf"), S2(A("Crate"), A("Shelf"))), S2(A("CrateHasSlot"), S2(A("Crate"), A("Slot")))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:ucs"), S1(S1(S4(A("UC:ep:CrateHasShelf#2+CrateHasSlot#2"), A("T"), A("F"), S2(S2(A("CrateHasShelf"), N(2)), S2(A("CrateHasSlot"), N(2))))))),
         S3(A("CELL"), A("state:alethic_clean"), A("T"))))),
"A FACT POST OVER A CLEAN STORE IS REFUSED FOR THE EXTERNAL UNIQUENESS IT BREAKS. Over a store known clean the fact POST, PUT and DELETE check only the constraints the write touched (ui:violations_in, through main:w2_viols and main:w2b_gate), and that list had no external uniqueness arm, while ui:violations and main:ab_viols_in, the assert path, run cmd:xuc_viols. Every compound reference scheme declares one (test:compound_keyed), so on a clean store a fact POST giving two Crates one Shelf and one Slot committed. Over test:xt_fx, which holds no alethic violation: a fact POST of c2 in Slot x1, which gives c2 the pair of c1, is refused 409 and its answer names the uniqueness violations of c1 and c2 over CrateHasShelf, the first member of UC:ep:CrateHasShelf#2+CrateHasSlot#2; a fact POST of c2 in Slot x2, a distinct pair, commits 201. Before ui:violations_in ran the arm, the first committed and this answered F.",
DEF("test:xuc_touched",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S5(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("main:alethic_of"), A("ui:violations"), N(1)),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), A("main:post_answer")), K(N(409)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), A("main:post_answer")), S3(A("COMP"), A("render:json"), K(S4(A("refused"), S2(S2(A("c2"), A("x1")), S2(A("c1"), A("x1"))), S2(S3(A("CrateHasShelf"), A("uniqueness"), S1(A("c2"))), S3(A("CrateHasShelf"), A("uniqueness"), S1(A("c1")))), PHI()))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), N(2), A("main:post_answer"), S4(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("CrateHasSlot")), K(S2(A("c2"), A("x2"))))), K(N(201))))),
       S4(A("CONS"), A("test:xt_fx"), K(A("CrateHasSlot")), K(S2(A("c2"), A("x1")))))),
"THE ROUND TRIP FIXTURE: one readings file declaring Crate identified by Crate`s Shelf and Slot, Shelf, Slot and Weight value types, Crate belongs to Shelf, Crate has Slot, Crate is fragile, and Crate has at most one Weight, with three Crates named S1/A, S1/B and S2/A whose components the readings state. test:cr_store is the store compile:check makes of it, each cell chunked as a compile files it.",
DEF("test:cr_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("crates.md"), A("Shelf is a value type.\nSlot is a value type.\nWeight is a value type.\nCrate(.Shelf, .Slot) is an entity type.\nCrate belongs to Shelf.\nCrate has Slot.\nCrate is fragile.\nCrate has Weight.\n  Each Crate has at most one Weight.\nCrate 'S1/A' belongs to Shelf 'S1'.\nCrate 'S1/A' has Slot 'A'.\nCrate 'S1/A' is fragile.\nCrate 'S1/A' has Weight 'heavy'.\nCrate 'S1/B' belongs to Shelf 'S1'.\nCrate 'S1/B' has Slot 'B'.\nCrate 'S1/B' has Weight 'light'.\nCrate 'S2/A' belongs to Shelf 'S2'.\nCrate 'S2/A' has Slot 'A'.\nCrate 'S2/A' is fragile.\n"), A("cr/crates.md"))))),
DEF("test:cr_store",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:cr_files"))),
DEF("test:cr_db",
    K(A("law-compound-roundtrip.db"))),
"<store> to <store, database>, the database made fresh; then the map laid out in it; then every table the map lays out filled with its rows, as a compile fills them.",
DEF("test:cr_s1",
    S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), A("test:cr_db")))),
DEF("test:cr_s2",
    S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:schema"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), N(1))))),
DEF("test:cr_s3",
    S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:sb_put_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:tables"), N(1)), N(2)))))),
"<database, store> to the facts the database reads back as a boot reads them: each table rmap:coltabs names, its rmap:proj_colnames columns, a wide entity table`s rows kept sparse, and every row through rmap:unproj or rmap:unproj_sp, as compile:ip_read_one and compile:ip_unproj read them.",
DEF("test:cr_read",
    S5(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:ip_unproj")), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:ip_read_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distl"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("rmap:coltabs"), N(2))))), N(2)))),
"<store, database, counts> to <store, facts read back, database>, and then the database cleared.",
DEF("test:cr_s4",
    S4(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_read"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), N(1))), N(2))),
DEF("test:cr_s5",
    S4(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(3)))),
"<fact type, facts> to the rows of that fact type among the facts. test:cr_same holds <store, facts> to T when every fact type`s population reads back equal to what was written; test:cr_back is the store with every fact type`s population replaced by what read back, as a boot adopts it through store:src_all.",
