"A COMPOUND-KEYED ENTITY`S FACTS ROUND-TRIP THROUGH STORAGE AS ITS REFERENCE. Measured on support through served verbs: after a check and compile, fact GET answered CostTierHasRateProvenance as BrightData, datacenter, invoice under two columns and ProviderResourceIsUnmapped as Fly.io, mda under one, and the validators reported a uniqueness violation on role 1 and a mandatory violation for every Cost Tier. The table of an entity with a compound reference scheme is keyed by the component columns, the populations name the instance by its reference, and the read took the key columns for the reference. test:cr_files is written through the storage interface to a fresh database, test:cr_db beside the process, read back the way a boot reads it, and the database cleared: every fact type`s population reads back equal to what was written, and the store a boot would adopt from what read back holds no alethic violation. Before the read could give back the reference, CrateHasWeight read back as S1, B, light and CrateIsFragile as S1, A, the component fact types read back nothing, the validators reported the uniqueness of CrateHasWeight on role 1 and the mandatory of CrateBelongsToShelf and CrateHasSlot for each Crate, and this answered F.",
"THE REFERENCE FIXTURE: Crate identified by its Shelf and Slot, with a Weight so that it keeps a table of its own, Item identified by its Code and packed in at most one Crate, and Crate inspected on Date, many to many, with three Crates, three Items and three inspections. test:crr_store is the store compile:check makes of it.",
DEF("test:crr_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("crates.md"), A("Shelf is a value type.\nSlot is a value type.\nCode is a value type.\nDate is a value type.\nWeight is a value type.\nCrate(.Shelf, .Slot) is an entity type.\nItem(.Code) is an entity type.\nCrate belongs to Shelf.\nCrate has Slot.\nCrate has Weight.\n  Each Crate has at most one Weight.\nCrate 'S1/A' has Weight 'heavy'.\nItem is packed in Crate.\n  Each Item is packed in at most one Crate.\nCrate is inspected on Date.\n  Each Crate, Date combination occurs at most once in the population of Crate is inspected on Date.\nCrate 'S1/A' belongs to Shelf 'S1'.\nCrate 'S1/A' has Slot 'A'.\nCrate 'S1/B' belongs to Shelf 'S1'.\nCrate 'S1/B' has Slot 'B'.\nCrate 'S2/A' belongs to Shelf 'S2'.\nCrate 'S2/A' has Slot 'A'.\nItem 'i1' is packed in Crate 'S1/A'.\nItem 'i2' is packed in Crate 'S1/B'.\nItem 'i3' is packed in Crate 'S2/A'.\nCrate 'S1/A' is inspected on Date 'd1'.\nCrate 'S1/B' is inspected on Date 'd1'.\nCrate 'S1/A' is inspected on Date 'd2'.\n"), A("cr/crates.md"))))),
DEF("test:crr_store",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:crr_files"))),
"test:schema_rows holds the rows of the Relational Schema (csdp.md) that rmap:schema_cells reads from the map of test:crr_store to literal rows: Crate keyed by Shelf and Slot, Item by its Code and packed in at most one Crate, and Crate is inspected on Date many to many. Ids are paths under the placeholder schema schema. Three tables, CrateIsInspectedOnDate primarily for its fact type and for the object type lambda objectifies it as; twelve columns at the positions rmap:coltabs lays out, each for the role of every fact type its path enters through, so a column unpacked from Crate`s compound reference is for the role of the referencing fact type and the role of Crate`s identifying fact type (Halpin step 4), and the column rmap:ctab_bridge adds to Crate`s own table is for the roles Crate plays in its identifying fact types, Crate belongs to Shelf`s and Crate has Slot`s first (csdp.md: each Column is for some Role; rmap:sc_br1 writes them); the primary key of each table, and the two references to Crate`s. Item`s crate, shelf and slot are not nullable, rightly: Item plays no fact role but Item is packed in Crate beside its reference, so that role is implied mandatory (Halpin: a role an object type alone plays, other than its reference roles, is implicitly mandatory unless the type is independent), which rmap:gmi records as `implied` for Item`s role and `none` for Crate`s in Crate has Weight. The answer must name exactly these fact types and, in each, exactly these rows.",
