    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sr_verdict"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:sr_want"), S3(A("COMP"), A("rmap:schema_cells"), A("test:crr_store"))))),
"test:ddl_rows held schema:ddl, the script rendered from the rows of the Relational Schema (csdp.md: Table, Column, Table Key, Table Reference), to rmap:ddl, the script rendered from the map rmap:coltabs keeps, byte for byte (it failed first with schema:ddl stubbed), over the store the report is given -- the base store, the metamodel`s own schema -- and over test:crr_store, Crate`s compound key and the references to it, and test:dv_store, a fully derived head rendered as a view.",
"AND THE BAR OUTLIVES WHAT IT WAS MEASURED AGAINST. With test:ddl_rows holding, every caller rendered schema:ddl and rmap:ddl, rmap:ddl:derive and the renderers under them had no caller but the law, so they are deleted and the law pins what they wrote: over the base store a script of 36,067 characters (36,119 after Object Type Instance is required orientation, instances.md, became the column objectTypeInstanceIsRequiredOrientation of the Function table, 52 characters; 36,840 when test:eng_forms made Failure succeeds Violation, whose second rule compares two Timestamps, a view rather than a table; 39,438 now, since test:recursive_view made Domain draws on Domain, Domain reaches Domain and Status reaches Status in State Machine Definition views over WITH RECURSIVE), 74 tables and 12 views, among them Table Key spans Column keyed by its roles in order, tableKeyId then columnId, where the columns stand by name; and over test:crr_store and test:dv_store the whole script, as rmap:ddl wrote it. With the keys rendered in column order instead (schema:pkcols for schema:pkorder) the script is as long and this answered F.",
DEF("test:ddl_rows",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:dr_base"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:ddl"), A("test:crr_store")), K(A("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Crate\" (\n    \"shelf\" TEXT,\n    \"slot\" TEXT,\n    \"crate\" TEXT,\n    \"weight\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"shelf\", \"slot\")\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"CrateIsInspectedOnDate\" (\n    \"date\" TEXT,\n    \"shelf\" TEXT,\n    \"slot\" TEXT,\n    \"crate\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"shelf\", \"slot\", \"date\")\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Item\" (\n    \"code\" TEXT,\n    \"crate\" TEXT,\n    \"shelf\" TEXT,\n    \"slot\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"code\")\n);")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:ddl"), A("test:dv_store")), K(A("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Club\" (\n    \"clubId\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"clubId\")\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"ClubHoldsVenue\" (\n    \"clubId\" TEXT,\n    \"venueId\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"clubId\", \"venueId\")\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Member\" (\n    \"memberId\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"memberId\")\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"MemberJoinsClub\" (\n    \"clubId\" TEXT,\n    \"memberId\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"memberId\", \"clubId\")\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Venue\" (\n    \"venueId\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"venueId\")\n);\n\nDROP VIEW IF EXISTS \"MemberAttendsVenue\";\nCREATE VIEW \"MemberAttendsVenue\" (\"memberId\", \"venueId\") AS SELECT * FROM (SELECT DISTINCT g.c1 AS c1, h.c2 AS c2 FROM (SELECT DISTINCT \"memberId\" AS c1, \"clubId\" AS c2 FROM \"MemberJoinsClub\" WHERE \"memberId\" IS NOT NULL AND \"clubId\" IS NOT NULL) AS g JOIN (SELECT DISTINCT \"clubId\" AS c1, \"venueId\" AS c2 FROM \"ClubHoldsVenue\" WHERE \"clubId\" IS NOT NULL AND \"venueId\" IS NOT NULL) AS h ON g.c2 = h.c1);"))))))),
DEF("test:dr_base",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("length"), A("chars"), A("schema:ddl")), K(N(39438)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S6(A("COMP"), A("length"), A("schema:dd_cls"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("t")), A("storage:render_rows")), A("schema:ddl_in"), A("schema:env")), K(N(74)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("length"), N(7), A("schema:env")), K(N(12)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("cn:contains"), S3(A("CONS"), A("schema:ddl"), K(A("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"TableKeySpansColumn\" (\n    \"columnId\" TEXT,\n    \"tableKeyId\" TEXT,\n    PRIMARY KEY (\"tableKeyId\", \"columnId\")\n);"))))))),
"test:ddl_sql holds the script SQLite renders from the rows of the Relational Schema (schema:render) to the one lambda`s renderers render from them (schema:ddl_text), byte for byte, over the base store`s schema, the fixtures` -- test:crr_store`s compound key and references, test:dv_store`s view, test:vk_store`s value type keyed by its value, test:kj_store`s mandatory -- and test:dl_a`s rows with a nullable column added and with a wider key. Run first with sqlite:render_rows answering no statement, it failed. AND THE BAR OUTLIVES WHAT IT WAS MEASURED AGAINST: with the two agreeing, schema:ddl rendered by SQLite, and lambda`s renderers -- schema:ddl_text, ddl_one, ddl_table, ddl_col, ddl_pk, colspec, sqltype, tabs, pkorder and those under them -- had no caller but the law, so they are deleted and the law pins what they wrote, each script by its SHA-256 digest (test:ds_pins); the base store`s digest moved when test:eng_forms made Failure succeeds Violation a view, and again when test:recursive_view made three heads that read themselves views over WITH RECURSIVE.",
DEF("test:ds_envs",
    S(A("CONS"), A("schema:env"), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:env"), A("test:crr_store")), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:env"), A("test:dv_store")), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:env"), A("test:vk_store")), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:env"), A("test:kj_store")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:env_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:dl_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dl_a"), A("test:dl_note"))), A("test:crr_store"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:env_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:dl_add"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dl_a"), A("test:dl_key"))), A("test:crr_store"))))),
