"test:value_key_role holds the key column of a value type`s own table to the role the value type plays in the fact types that table carries (csdp.md: each Column is for some Role). A value type is a concept type, and gets a table, only where it plays a role no entity`s table absorbs (rmap:vtcts), and that table is keyed by the one identifier step rmap:b3pidchains gives it, an info step through no fact type, so the column it lays out holds the value itself and rmap:schema_cells left it for no Role -- measured in claude`s store, claude:Email:value and claude:Polarity:value, the only Columns of it for none. The fixture is that shape twice: Email, which exactly one User has, so UserHasEmail is grouped on Email`s side and Email`s table carries it, and Polarity, opposite to at most one Polarity, a ring Polarity`s table carries. Over the schema rows of the store compile:check makes of it, Email`s value column is for UserHasEmail.2, Polarity`s for PolarityIsOppositeToPolarity.1, the role beside the ring`s column, which is for its second; every Column is for some Role; and the fact type each column carries, as storage:schema_map reads the map back, is as before those rows were written: the user column carries UserHasEmail, the polarity column the ring, and neither value column carries anything, since a value column holds the subject of its table, which is read back as the row and not as a fact. Run first with the fix absent, the value columns were for no Role and this answered F.",
