    S4(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_verdict"), S6(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_s5"), A("test:cr_s4"), A("test:cr_s3"), A("test:cr_s2"), A("test:cr_s1")), A("test:crr_store"))),
"THE BARE FIXTURE: Crate identified by its Shelf and Slot and nothing else, no fact of its own beyond its components and no role in any other fact type, with three Crates, and beside it Item identified by its Code with at most one Color, unrelated to Crate, so that the database has a table to make. test:crn_store is the store compile:check makes of it.",
DEF("test:crn_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("crates.md"), A("Shelf is a value type.\nSlot is a value type.\nCode is a value type.\nColor is a value type.\nCrate(.Shelf, .Slot) is an entity type.\nItem(.Code) is an entity type.\nCrate belongs to Shelf.\nCrate has Slot.\nItem has Color.\n  Each Item has at most one Color.\nItem 'i1' has Color 'red'.\nCrate 'S1/A' belongs to Shelf 'S1'.\nCrate 'S1/A' has Slot 'A'.\nCrate 'S1/B' belongs to Shelf 'S1'.\nCrate 'S1/B' has Slot 'B'.\nCrate 'S2/A' belongs to Shelf 'S2'.\nCrate 'S2/A' has Slot 'A'.\n"), A("cr/crates.md"))))),
DEF("test:crn_store",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:crn_files"))),
"A COMPOUND-IDENTIFIED ENTITY WITH NO FACT BEYOND ITS COMPONENTS IS STORED. The map gave an entity a table only when it had a fact to hold beyond its identification, so Crate identified by its Shelf and Slot and nothing else had no table, and its component facts, Crate belongs to Shelf and Crate has Slot, were written nowhere: a store read back from its tables lost every Crate. test:crn_files written through the storage interface, read back as a boot reads it and the database cleared, as test:compound_roundtrip does: every fact type`s population reads back equal to what was written, and the adopted store holds no alethic violation. Before such an entity had a table, CrateBelongsToShelf and CrateHasSlot read back nothing, and this answered F.",
