DEF("test:cm_db",
    K(A("law-compound-migrate.db"))),
"<store, runtime facts> to <store, the runtime`s store laid out the old way, the readings` store laid out the old way, database>, the database made fresh; then the old map laid out in it, its ledgers opened, every table filled with the runtime`s store`s rows, and _readings filled with the facts the readings` store holds, as the last compile wrote them.",
DEF("test:cm_o1",
    S5(A("CONS"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cm_old"), A("test:cm_with")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cm_old"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), A("test:cm_db")))),
DEF("test:cm_o2",
    S6(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3), N(4), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:schema"), S3(A("CONS"), N(4), N(2))))),
DEF("test:cm_o3",
    S6(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3), N(4), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:meta"), N(4)))),
DEF("test:cm_o4",
    S6(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3), N(4), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:sb_put_one")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:tables"), N(2)), N(4)))))),
DEF("test:cm_o5",
    S6(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), N(3), N(4), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:put"), S5(A("CONS"), N(4), K(A("_readings")), K(S2(A("ft"), A("row"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:facts_of"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:tables"), N(3)), N(3))))))),
DEF("test:cm_run",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("test:cm_o5"), A("test:cm_o4"), A("test:cm_o3"), A("test:cm_o2"), A("test:cm_o1"))),
"<store, old store, ...> to what the in-place compile reads the old store through: <database, the old map`s store, the new store, no table left unread>.",
DEF("test:cm_x",
    S5(A("CONS"), N(4), N(3), N(1), K(PHI()))),
"<staged tuple> to the facts the in-place compile reads out of every table of the old map, one table at a time by compile:ip_old_table, and then the database cleared.",
DEF("test:cm_read",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:ip_old_table")), S3(A("COMP"), A("distr"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("rmap:coltabs"), N(3)), A("test:cm_x")))), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(4))))),
"<staged tuple> to the rows of the old store compile:ip_unref names as having no reference to be read by, and then the database cleared.",
DEF("test:cm_unref",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ip_unref"), A("test:cm_x")), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(4))))),
"<new store> to T when the old store with test:cm_ok reads back as the new store with those facts, every population equal.",
DEF("test:cm_a",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_same"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cm_with"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:cm_ok"))), S4(A("COMP"), A("test:cm_read"), A("test:cm_run"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:cm_ok")))))),
"<new store> to T when the new store with test:cm_ok, written through the storage interface in the new layout and read back as a boot reads it, holds every population and no alethic violation.",
DEF("test:cm_w",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_verdict"), S6(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_s5"), A("test:cr_s4"), A("test:cr_s3"), A("test:cr_s2"), A("test:cr_s1")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cm_with"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:cm_ok"))))),
"<new store> to T when the old store with test:cm_bad names exactly one row with no reference to be read by, the row of C/z.",
DEF("test:cm_b",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("COMP"), A("and"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("length"), K(N(1)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("cn:contains"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("C, z")))))), A("test:cm_unref"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cm_run"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:cm_bad"))))),
"A STORE THE OLD LAYOUT WROTE MIGRATES UNDER THE NEW ONE. Measured on a copy of support: the check of support failed in the in-place compile with SQLite query expected 5 values, received 6, row 1 of 7 beginning BrightData, us_datacenters_static_ip. The store`s Cost Tier table was written by the map before a compound-keyed table kept its reference, so it has no reference column, and the compile reads such a table through the old map, where the key is the components. test:cm_files is written to test:cm_db by the old map, the runtime`s facts beside the readings` and _readings holding the readings`, as the last compile wrote it. Read back by compile:ip_old_table, the in-place compile`s read of an old table, every population must equal the new store`s with the runtime`s facts, the reference of each Cost Tier the readings identify taken from the readings; written by the new map and read back, the same store must hold every population and no alethic violation; and where the runtime made a Cost Tier no reading names, compile:ip_unref must name that row, as the check reports it, rather than invent a reference or drop it. Before the old table was read into the new layout, the first answered F, and this answered F.",
DEF("test:compound_migrate",
    S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("COND"), A("test:cm_a"), S4(A("COND"), A("test:cm_w"), A("test:cm_b"), K(A("F"))), K(A("F"))), A("test:cm_new"))),
"THE NESTED FIXTURE, as support declares Provider Resource: Provider Resource identified by its Cost Center and its Resource Name, Cost Center an entity identified by its Center Name, so one component reaches its value through two steps; Service identified by its Service Name; Provider Resource supports Service, many to many; and Provider Resource is unmapped. test:cn_store is the store compile:check makes of it.",
DEF("test:cn_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("res.md"), A("Center Name is a value type.\nResource Name is a value type.\nService Name is a value type.\nCost Center(.Center Name) is an entity type.\nService(.Service Name) is an entity type.\nProvider Resource(.Cost Center, .Resource Name) is an entity type.\nProvider Resource has Cost Center.\nProvider Resource has Resource Name.\nProvider Resource supports Service.\n  Each Provider Resource, Service combination occurs at most once in the population of Provider Resource supports Service.\nProvider Resource is unmapped.\nProvider Resource 'F/a' has Cost Center 'F'.\nProvider Resource 'F/a' has Resource Name 'a'.\nProvider Resource 'F/b' has Cost Center 'F'.\nProvider Resource 'F/b' has Resource Name 'b'.\nProvider Resource 'C/a' has Cost Center 'C'.\nProvider Resource 'C/a' has Resource Name 'a'.\nProvider Resource 'F/a' supports Service 's1'.\nProvider Resource 'F/b' supports Service 's1'.\nProvider Resource 'C/a' is unmapped.\n"), A("cn/res.md"))))),
DEF("test:cn_store",
    S6(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("compile:cellify")), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:cn_files"))),
"A ROLE OF AN ENTITY WHOSE COMPONENT IS ITSELF AN ENTITY ROUND-TRIPS AS ITS REFERENCE. Measured on a copy of support after the in-place compile: ProviderResourceSupportsService read back as Fly.io, src.do and ClickHouse, src.do twice, the first component of each Provider Resource, because Cost Center reaches its value through has Cost Center and then has Center Name, the role`s two component columns did not share the path less its last step, and no reference column stood beside them. test:cn_files written through the storage interface and read back as a boot reads it, as test:compound_roundtrip does: every population reads back equal to what was written and the adopted store holds no alethic violation. With the role`s columns grouped by the path less its last step, ProviderResourceSupportsService read back as F, s1 twice and this answered F, measured with rmap:compound_fts answering nothing.",
DEF("test:compound_nested",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_verdict"), S6(A("COMP"), A("test:cr_s5"), A("test:cr_s4"), A("test:cr_s3"), A("test:cr_s2"), A("test:cr_s1")), A("test:cn_store"))),
"A FUNCTION IS DECLARED IN ONE DOMAIN, AND A SECOND IS A DEONTIC VIOLATION THAT WARNS. Function belongs to Domain holds at most one Domain, so a second declaration had no row to be; Function is declared in Domain holds one row per Domain that declares the Function, and the obligation that each Function is declared in at most one Domain is decided by decide:declared_once, so a collision warns and commits and is never refused. test:decided_declared_once holds the decider`s rule, decide:dio_rows, to literal rows <Function, Domain>: f1 in alpha and beta, f2 in alpha twice, f3 in gamma, and it answers f1 alone. test:declared_in reads gx/c.md and then the two fx files of test:local_names, so fx is the level read last: with the path ids (compile:path_dups) the reflection of FunctionIsDeclaredInDomain holds alpha:Gizmo in alpha and beta:Gizmo in beta, two Functions each declared once, no row for the bare Gizmo and none in gamma, which the cascade overrode, and the decider`s rule answers nothing; before them it held Gizmo in alpha and in beta and the rule answered Gizmo. test:declared_once reads two files at one level that both declare Gizmo in alpha: the population holds Gizmo in alpha, and the rule answers nothing. The rule is asked only once decide:declared_once is in decide:deciders. Before the population and the decider exist, the three laws answer F.",
DEF("test:decided_declared_once",
    S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("decide:declared_once")), A("decide:deciders"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("apply"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("decide:dio_rows")), K(S5(S2(A("f1"), A("alpha")), S2(A("f1"), A("beta")), S2(A("f2"), A("alpha")), S2(A("f2"), A("alpha")), S2(A("f3"), A("gamma")))))),
          K(S1(A("f1"))))),
       K(A("F")))),
DEF("test:di_two_files",
    K(S3(S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("gx/c.md")),
         S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget is labeled.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("fx/a.md")),
         S3(A("b.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nDomain 'beta' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("fx/b.md"))))),
DEF("test:di_one_files",
    K(S2(S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("fx/a.md")),
         S3(A("b.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'alpha' has Description 'one domain'.\n"), A("fx/b.md"))))),
"<files>: the reflection of FunctionIsDeclaredInDomain over the cells compile:of_x answers for them, none while reflect:arms has no arm for it.",
DEF("test:di_arm",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FunctionIsDeclaredInDomain")), A("reflect:arms")))),
DEF("test:di_rows",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:di_arm")), K(PHI()),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("apply"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:di_arm"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2)))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair"))))),
DEF("test:di_listed",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("decide:declared_once")), A("decide:deciders")))),
"<rows>: what decide:dio_rows answers for them once the decider is listed, # before.",
DEF("test:di_decide",
    S4(A("COND"), A("test:di_listed"), S3(A("COMP"), A("apply"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("decide:dio_rows")), A("id"))), K(A("#")))),
DEF("test:declared_in",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S6(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:Gizmo"), A("alpha"))), A("id"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("beta:Gizmo"), A("beta"))), A("id"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("csdp:matches"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Gizmo")), A("id")))),
       A("test:di_listed"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:di_decide"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:di_rows"), A("test:di_two_files"))))),
DEF("test:declared_once",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Gizmo"), A("alpha"))), A("id"))),
       A("test:di_listed"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:di_decide"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:di_rows"), A("test:di_one_files"))))),

"A NAME RESOLVES IN ITS OWN DOMAIN FIRST, THEN IN THE DOMAINS IT REACHES, AND TWO OF THOSE ARE AMBIGUOUS. Namespacing is done by domain, not by hacking up the name, and a name from a library outside one`s control gets namespaced to disambiguate. core.md declares Domain reaches Domain, derived from Domain is contained in Domain and closed transitively, and that relation is the reach. A reading in a Domain that names a declared name resolves it to the declaration in that Domain; failing one, to the declaration in a Domain it reaches; and when two Domains it reaches declare the name and it does not, the reference is ambiguous, a finding of the check naming both Domains, and neither is picked. test:domain_resolve reads three files at one level: rx/a.md declares Gizmo, Widget and Sprocket under alpha; rx/b.md declares Sprocket under beta; rx/c.md declares Gizmo under gamma, speaks of Gizmo g1, Widget w1 and Sprocket s1, and says that gamma uses alpha and alpha uses beta, so gamma draws on alpha and beta (names travel by use, not by containment). Over what compile:check answers for them, state:resolutions holds <Gizmo, gamma, gamma> and not <Gizmo, gamma, alpha>, since gamma declares Gizmo itself; it holds <Widget, gamma, alpha>, since only alpha declares Widget; it holds no row for Sprocket; and the findings name exactly one ambiguous reference, Sprocket, with the Domains alpha and beta. Before the check resolves a name, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:dr_files",
    K(S3(S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nSprocket(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("rx/a.md")),
         S3(A("b.md"), A("Sprocket(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'beta' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("rx/b.md")),
         S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo is labeled.\nWidget is labeled.\nSprocket is labeled.\nGizmo 'g1' is labeled.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nSprocket 's1' is labeled.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'gamma' uses Domain 'alpha'.\nDomain 'alpha' uses Domain 'beta'.\n"), A("rx/c.md"))))),
"<cells, findings> of test:dr_files, as compile:check answers them for files it reads.",
DEF("test:dr_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:dr_files")))),
DEF("test:dr_res",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:resolutions")), N(1)))),
DEF("test:dr_amb",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(A("ambiguous")))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI()))), N(2))),
DEF("test:domain_resolve",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S8(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Gizmo"), A("gamma"), A("gamma"))), A("test:dr_res"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Gizmo"), A("gamma"), A("alpha"))), A("test:dr_res")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Widget"), A("gamma"), A("alpha"))), A("test:dr_res"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("csdp:matches"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Sprocket")), A("test:dr_res")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("test:dr_amb")), K(S1(A("Sprocket"))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:dr_amb")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), N(4), N(1), A("test:dr_amb")), K(S2(A("alpha"), A("beta")))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:dr_amb")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1), A("test:dr_amb")), K(A("reported")))))),
       A("test:dr_run")))),

"TWO FUNCTIONS WITH ONE NAME IN TWO DOMAINS ARE TWO THINGS, EACH IDENTIFIED BY ITS PATH. The Domain provides the namespace; the id is the computed path from Domain and Local Name, and namespacing is done by domain, not by hacking up the name. core.md: for each Domain and Local Name at most one Function belongs to that Domain and has that Local Name, and the colon notation denotes the path, the Domain then the cell in it. test:path_ids reads three files at one level: px/a.md declares Gizmo and Widget under alpha and says Gizmo g1 is shiny and Widget w1 is labeled; px/c.md declares Gizmo under gamma and says Gizmo g2 is labeled. No file is renamed and no name is prefixed in a reading. Over what compile:check answers for them: state:otmeta names alpha:Gizmo and gamma:Gizmo and not Gizmo, and still names Widget; the reflection of Function is declared in Domain holds alpha:Gizmo in alpha and gamma:Gizmo in gamma and no row for the bare Gizmo, and Widget in alpha; the reflection of Function has Local Name holds Gizmo as the Local Name of both path ids, and Widget as its own; and the classification (Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type, which px/m.md declares under meta so the reader reflects it; state:otpops is gone) files g1 under alpha:Gizmo alone, g2 under gamma:Gizmo alone, and nothing under the bare Gizmo. A name declared once keeps its id. Before a declaration has its path id, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:pi_files",
    K(S3(S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo is shiny.\nGizmo 'g1' is shiny.\nWidget is labeled.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("px/a.md")),
         S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo is labeled.\nGizmo 'g2' is labeled.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("px/c.md")),
         S3(A("m.md"), A("Object Type Instance(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Type(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\nDomain 'meta' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("px/m.md"))))),
"The cells compile:of_x answers for test:pi_files.",
DEF("test:pi_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:pi_files")))),
"<cells> to the names state:otmeta declares.",
DEF("test:pi_ots",
    S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:otmeta")), A("id")))),
"<arm name, cells> to what that arm of reflect:arms answers over the cells as a store.",
DEF("test:pi_arm",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("apply"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), A("reflect:arms"))), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))), N(2))))),
DEF("test:pi_di",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pi_arm"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FunctionIsDeclaredInDomain")), A("id")))),
DEF("test:pi_ln",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pi_arm"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("FunctionHasLocalName")), A("id")))),
"<type, cells> to the instances the classification files under that type (ui:ids over the cells as a store: Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type, which px/m.md declares so the reader reflects it).",
DEF("test:pi_pop",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:ids"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))), N(2)), N(1)))),
DEF("test:path_ids",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:Gizmo")), A("test:pi_ots"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:Gizmo")), A("test:pi_ots"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Gizmo")), A("test:pi_ots")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Widget")), A("test:pi_ots"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:Gizmo"), A("alpha"))), A("test:pi_di"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("gamma:Gizmo"), A("gamma"))), A("test:pi_di"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("csdp:matches"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Gizmo")), A("test:pi_di")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Widget"), A("alpha"))), A("test:pi_di"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:Gizmo"), A("Gizmo"))), A("test:pi_ln"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("gamma:Gizmo"), A("Gizmo"))), A("test:pi_ln"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Widget"), A("Widget"))), A("test:pi_ln"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pi_pop"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:Gizmo")), A("id"))), K(S1(A("g1"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pi_pop"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:Gizmo")), A("id"))), K(S1(A("g2"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pi_pop"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Gizmo")), A("id"))))),
       A("test:pi_run")))),

"A FACT TYPE OVER A NAME DECLARED IN TWO DOMAINS IS READ OVER THE DECLARATION ITS DOMAIN RESOLVES TO, AND THE MAP KEEPS THE TWO APART. A player named in a reading resolves as an instance reference does: to the declaration in the Domain of its file, else to the one declaration in a Domain it reaches (core.md, Domain reaches Domain). test:path_fts reads three files at one level: qx/b.md declares the value type Color under base; qx/a.md declares Gizmo under alpha and reads Gizmo has Color, each Gizmo with at most one Color, and says alpha uses base; qx/c.md says the same under gamma. Over what compile:check answers for them: state:fts holds a fact type whose players are alpha:Gizmo and Color and one whose players are gamma:Gizmo and Color, and none over the bare Gizmo; and the map keys a table for alpha:Gizmo and one for gamma:Gizmo, and none for the bare Gizmo. The law names no fact type id, since how one is minted from a player that is a path is not yet the metamodel`s to say. Before a reading resolves its players, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:pf_files",
    K(S3(S3(A("b.md"), A("Color is a value type.\nDomain 'base' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("qx/b.md")),
         S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo has Color.\n  Each Gizmo has at most one Color.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'alpha' uses Domain 'base'.\n"), A("qx/a.md")),
         S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo has Color.\n  Each Gizmo has at most one Color.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'gamma' uses Domain 'base'.\n"), A("qx/c.md"))))),
"The cells compile:of_x answers for test:pf_files.",
DEF("test:pf_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:pf_files")))),
