DEF("test:pf_players",
    S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))),
"<cells> to the tables the map keys over the cells as a store.",
DEF("test:pf_tables",
    S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("rmap:pkrows"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))))),
DEF("test:path_fts",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S7(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:Gizmo"), A("Color"))), A("test:pf_players"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("gamma:Gizmo"), A("Color"))), A("test:pf_players"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Gizmo"), A("Color"))), A("test:pf_players")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:Gizmo")), A("test:pf_tables"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:Gizmo")), A("test:pf_tables"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Gizmo")), A("test:pf_tables"))))),
       A("test:pf_run")))),

"A FACT TYPE HAS THE DOMAIN WHOSE FILE READS IT, AND ITS ID IS THE PATH WHEN ITS LOCAL NAME IS READ IN TWO DOMAINS. Fact types have domains: they map to tables and columns. A fact type is a Function: it belongs to the Domain whose file reads it, its Local Name is the cell name minted from its reading, and by core.md:781 its id is d:L exactly when L is read in more than one Domain at one level; a fact type read once keeps its bare id, and roles, reference modes and constraints follow from that id by the conventions they already have. test:path_ft_ids reads three files at one level: qy/b.md declares Color and Widget under base; qy/a.md declares Gizmo under alpha, reads Gizmo has Color, each Gizmo with at most one Color, and Widget is popular, and says alpha uses base; qy/c.md the same under gamma. Over what compile:check answers: state:fts names alpha:GizmoHasColor and gamma:GizmoHasColor and not GizmoHasColor; it names alpha:WidgetIsPopular and gamma:WidgetIsPopular and not WidgetIsPopular, a reading restated in a second Domain being a second fact type; state:schemereadings names the reference fact types alpha:GizmoHasGizmoId and gamma:GizmoHasGizmoId; and the map walks alpha:GizmoHasColor from the alpha:Gizmo table and gamma:GizmoHasColor from the gamma:Gizmo table. Before a fact type is minted by its Domain, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:pt_files",
    K(S3(S3(A("b.md"), A("Color is a value type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'base' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("qy/b.md")),
         S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo has Color.\n  Each Gizmo has at most one Color.\nWidget is popular.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'alpha' uses Domain 'base'.\n"), A("qy/a.md")),
         S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo has Color.\n  Each Gizmo has at most one Color.\nWidget is popular.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'gamma' uses Domain 'base'.\n"), A("qy/c.md"))))),
"The cells compile:of_x answers for test:pt_files.",
DEF("test:pt_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:pt_files")))),
"<cell name, cells> to the first element of each row of that cell.",
DEF("test:pt_ids",
    S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), A("solve:assoc"))),
"<table, cells> to the fact types the map walks from that table, over the cells as a store.",
DEF("test:pt_walk",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:tab_facts"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), S4(A("COMP"), A("rmap:ctab"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))), N(2))))),
DEF("test:path_ft_ids",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:GizmoHasColor")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:GizmoHasColor")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("GizmoHasColor")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:WidgetIsPopular")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:WidgetIsPopular")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("WidgetIsPopular")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:GizmoHasGizmoId")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:schemereadings")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:GizmoHasGizmoId")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_ids"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:schemereadings")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:GizmoHasColor")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_walk"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("alpha:Gizmo")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:GizmoHasColor")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:pt_walk"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("gamma:Gizmo")), A("id")))))),
       A("test:pt_run")))),

"A RING CONSTRAINT IS VERBALIZED AS HALPIN WRITES IT. A ring constraint must be verbalized properly. verbalization.md reads a ring in the fact type`s own words, `Domain uses Domain is acyclic.`, and FORML 2 says what it means: Halpin, Information Modeling and Relational Databases, and NORMA`s ring verbalizations, with subscripts telling the players apart. Over Domain uses Domain: irreflexive, No Domain uses itself; asymmetric, If Domain1 uses Domain2 then it is impossible that Domain2 uses Domain1; antisymmetric, If Domain1 uses Domain2 and Domain1 is not Domain2 then it is impossible that Domain2 uses Domain1; symmetric, If Domain1 uses Domain2 then Domain2 uses Domain1; intransitive, If Domain1 uses Domain2 and Domain2 uses Domain3 then it is impossible that Domain1 uses Domain3; transitive, If Domain1 uses Domain2 and Domain2 uses Domain3 then Domain1 uses Domain3; acyclic, No Domain may cycle back to itself via one or more traversals through Domain uses Domain. Each is the Text of the ring Constraint, written as every Text of the store is, with no final period. The seven kinds are the Constraint Types core.md names; Reflexive (RF) has no Name there, so no ring is read as it. test:ring_verbal reads rv/r.md, which declares Domain uses Domain with a ring of each kind and names the seven Constraint Types: over its cells as a store, the reflection of Constraint has Text answers exactly those seven sentences, each the Text of a Constraint the reflection of Constraint is of Constraint Type answers. Before the reflection gives a ring its Text, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:rv_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("r.md"), A("Function(.id) is an entity type.\nConstraint Type is a subtype of Function.\nName is a value type.\nFunction has Name.\n  Each Function has at most one Name.\nConstraint Type 'IR' has Name 'Irreflexive'.\nConstraint Type 'AS' has Name 'Asymmetric'.\nConstraint Type 'AT' has Name 'Antisymmetric'.\nConstraint Type 'SY' has Name 'Symmetric'.\nConstraint Type 'IT' has Name 'Intransitive'.\nConstraint Type 'TR' has Name 'Transitive'.\nConstraint Type 'AC' has Name 'Acyclic'.\nDomain(.Name) is an entity type.\nDomain uses Domain.\nDomain uses Domain is irreflexive.\nDomain uses Domain is asymmetric.\nDomain uses Domain is antisymmetric.\nDomain uses Domain is symmetric.\nDomain uses Domain is intransitive.\nDomain uses Domain is transitive.\nDomain uses Domain is acyclic.\nDomain 'rv' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("rv/r.md"))))),
DEF("test:rv_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:rv_files")))),
"<arm name, cells> to what that arm of reflect:arms answers over the cells as a store with its FILE built (main:refile), as a store a start makes has one, none when there is no such arm.",
DEF("test:rv_arm",
    S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), A("reflect:arms")))), K(PHI()),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("apply"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), A("reflect:arms"))), S4(A("COMP"), A("main:refile"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))), N(2)))))),
DEF("test:ring_verbal",
    S5(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), K(S7(
          A("No Domain uses itself"),
          A("If Domain1 uses Domain2 then it is impossible that Domain2 uses Domain1"),
          A("If Domain1 uses Domain2 and Domain1 is not Domain2 then it is impossible that Domain2 uses Domain1"),
          A("If Domain1 uses Domain2 then Domain2 uses Domain1"),
          A("If Domain1 uses Domain2 and Domain2 uses Domain3 then it is impossible that Domain1 uses Domain3"),
          A("If Domain1 uses Domain2 and Domain2 uses Domain3 then Domain1 uses Domain3"),
          A("No Domain may cycle back to itself via one or more traversals through Domain uses Domain")))), N(1)),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:subset"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), N(2))), A("id"))),
       S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rv_arm"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintHasText")), A("id"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rv_arm"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintIsOfConstraintType")), A("id")))),
       A("test:rv_run"))),

"A FACT STATED TWICE IS ONE FACT. Under ORM`s set semantics a population is a set: a sentence restated, in its own file or in a file of another Domain, adds no row, and identical rows can never violate a uniqueness constraint. test:dup_facts reads two files at two levels: dx/core/c.md declares under core the fact types Object Type has Conceptual Data Type, Object Type is of Object Kind and Object Type has Enum Values, each Object Type with at most one of each, the value type Title, whose data type is text, and the value type Coverage Region, whose possible values are 'US' and 'EU'; dx/app/s.md, under sherlock, declares Explanation(.Title) and restates that the data type of Title is text, restates Coverage Region and its possible values, and declares Authority(.citation) and Law(.citation), saying twice that the data type of citation is text. support.auto.dev`s store held each shape: sherlock.md restates core`s data types of Title and Description, vendored-deps.md says six times that the data type of citation is text and restates api-products.md`s values of Coverage Region. Over the cells compile:check answers for them, as a store: the population of Object Type has Conceptual Data Type holds <Title, text> and <citation, text>, that of Object Type has Enum Values holds <Coverage Region, 'US', 'EU'>, and none of the three populations holds a row twice; and the check of the store (ui:violations) answers no uniqueness violation. Before a restated declaration is read as one fact, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:df_files",
    K(S2(S3(A("c.md"), A("Object Type(.id) is an entity type.\nConceptual Data Type(.id) is an entity type.\nObject Kind is a value type.\nObject Type has Conceptual Data Type.\n  Each Object Type has at most one Conceptual Data Type.\nObject Type is of Object Kind.\n  Each Object Type is of at most one Object Kind.\nEnum Values is a value type.\nObject Type has Enum Values.\n  Each Object Type has at most one Enum Values.\nTitle is a value type.\n  The data type of Title is text.\nCoverage Region is a value type.\n  The possible values of Coverage Region are 'US', 'EU'.\nDomain 'core' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("dx/core/c.md")),
         S3(A("s.md"), A("Explanation(.Title) is an entity type.\n  The data type of Title is text.\nCoverage Region is a value type.\n  The possible values of Coverage Region are 'US', 'EU'.\nAuthority(.citation) is an entity type.\n  The data type of citation is text.\nLaw(.citation) is an entity type.\n  The data type of citation is text.\nDomain 'sherlock' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("dx/app/s.md"))))),
"The cells compile:of_x answers for test:df_files, as a store with its FILE built (main:refile).",
DEF("test:df_run",
    S6(A("COMP"), A("main:refile"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), N(2))), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:df_files")))),
"<fact type, store> to its population.",
DEF("test:df_rows",
    A("system:pop_rows")),
"<rows> to whether no row is in them twice.",
DEF("test:df_set",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), A("length"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), A("theta:dedup"))))),
DEF("test:dup_facts",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S8(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Title"), A("text"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeHasConceptualDataType")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("Coverage Region"), A("'US', 'EU'"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeHasEnumValues")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_set"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeHasEnumValues")), A("id")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("citation"), A("text"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeHasConceptualDataType")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_set"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeHasConceptualDataType")), A("id")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_set"), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:df_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeIsOfObjectKind")), A("id")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("uniqueness")))), S2(A("CONS"), A("id")), K(PHI()))), A("ui:violations")))),
       A("test:df_run")))),

"A NAME RESOLVES THROUGH THE DOMAINS ITS DOMAIN DRAWS ON, AND NEVER THROUGH CONTAINMENT. core.md: Domain uses Domain is a library import, for names only; Domain draws on Domain is its transitive closure; and Domain reaches Domain is data addressing, parent into child, which names do not travel by. A name resolves in its own Domain, then in the Domains it draws on, and two of those are ambiguous. test:domain_uses reads four files at one level: ux/a.md declares Gizmo, Widget and Sprocket under alpha, which uses beta; ux/b.md declares Sprocket under beta; ux/c.md declares Gizmo under gamma, which uses alpha, and speaks of Gizmo g1, Widget w1 and Sprocket s1; ux/d.md is delta, contained in alpha, and speaks of Widget w2. Over what compile:check answers: state:resolutions holds <Gizmo, gamma, gamma>, its own Domain first, and <Widget, gamma, alpha>, which gamma uses; it holds no row for Sprocket in gamma, which draws on alpha and, through it, beta, and the findings name that reference ambiguous with the Domains alpha and beta; and it holds no row <Widget, delta, alpha>, since delta is contained in alpha and uses nothing. Before the check reads uses, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:du_files",
    K(S4(S3(A("a.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nWidget(.id) is an entity type.\nSprocket(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'alpha' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'alpha' uses Domain 'beta'.\n"), A("ux/a.md")),
         S3(A("b.md"), A("Sprocket(.id) is an entity type.\nDomain 'beta' has Access 'public'.\n"), A("ux/b.md")),
         S3(A("c.md"), A("Gizmo(.id) is an entity type.\nGizmo is labeled.\nWidget is labeled.\nSprocket is labeled.\nGizmo 'g1' is labeled.\nWidget 'w1' is labeled.\nSprocket 's1' is labeled.\nDomain 'gamma' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'gamma' uses Domain 'alpha'.\n"), A("ux/c.md")),
         S3(A("d.md"), A("Widget 'w2' is labeled.\nDomain 'delta' has Access 'public'.\nDomain 'delta' is contained in Domain 'alpha'.\n"), A("ux/d.md"))))),
"<cells, findings> of test:du_files, as compile:check answers them for files it reads.",
DEF("test:du_run",
    S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:du_files")))),
DEF("test:domain_uses",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S7(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Gizmo"), A("gamma"), A("gamma"))), A("test:dr_res"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Widget"), A("gamma"), A("alpha"))), A("test:dr_res"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Widget"), A("delta"), A("alpha"))), A("test:dr_res")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("csdp:matches"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Sprocket")), A("test:dr_res")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), A("test:dr_amb")), K(S1(A("Sprocket"))))),
       S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("test:dr_amb")), K(A("F")), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), N(4), N(1), A("test:dr_amb")), K(S2(A("alpha"), A("beta"))))))),
       A("test:du_run")))),

"A FACT TYPE WHOSE ID IS A PATH HAS ITS LOCAL NAME AND ITS DOMAIN OF DECLARATION, AS AN OBJECT TYPE DOES. core.md: each Function has at most one Local Name, and Function is declared in Domain holds one row per Domain that declares it. A fact type read in two Domains is two Functions, d:L in each (test:path_ft_ids), and the reflection gave neither a Local Name nor a Domain of declaration, since state:localnames records object types and instances. test:ft_reflected reads test:pt_files: over the cells as a store, the reflection of Function has Local Name holds <alpha:GizmoHasColor, GizmoHasColor>, <gamma:GizmoHasColor, GizmoHasColor>, <alpha:WidgetIsPopular, WidgetIsPopular> and <gamma:WidgetIsPopular, WidgetIsPopular>, and the reflection of Function is declared in Domain holds each of the four in its own Domain. Before the reflection reads a fact type`s Domain, the law answers F.",
DEF("test:ft_reflected",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S9(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:GizmoHasColor"), A("GizmoHasColor"))), A("test:pi_ln"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("gamma:GizmoHasColor"), A("GizmoHasColor"))), A("test:pi_ln"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:WidgetIsPopular"), A("WidgetIsPopular"))), A("test:pi_ln"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("gamma:WidgetIsPopular"), A("WidgetIsPopular"))), A("test:pi_ln"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:GizmoHasColor"), A("alpha"))), A("test:pi_di"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("gamma:GizmoHasColor"), A("gamma"))), A("test:pi_di"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("alpha:WidgetIsPopular"), A("alpha"))), A("test:pi_di"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("gamma:WidgetIsPopular"), A("gamma"))), A("test:pi_di")))),
       A("test:pt_run")))),

"test:typed_cols holds sqlite:typed_cols to the base store`s own tables: Function`s key functionId and belongsToDomainId (Function belongs to Domain, an entity type) are columns an entity can stand in, its description and localName (value types) are not, and DomainReachesDomain, a relation over two Domains, keeps both its columns.",
DEF("test:typed_cols",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S6(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("functionId")), N(1))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("belongsToDomainId")), N(1))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("description")), N(1))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("localName")), N(1))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("length"), N(2)), K(N(2)))))),
       S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:typed_cols"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Function")), A("id"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("sqlite:typed_cols"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("DomainReachesDomain")), A("id")))))),
"test:nest_place holds the in-place compile`s read of an attribute of an objectified fact type whose table is keyed by the objectification`s roles and holds no reference column: support`s Plan Product, Plan Product objectifies `Plan includes Platform API`, keyed by plan and platformAPI, with its per-call Amount beside them (on a copy of support`s store, once the columns carried their own fact types, the in-place check still refused PlanProductHasPerCallAmount as reading back none of the facts the last readings asserted, Plan Product `Growth.apr` has per-call Amount `0.005` among them). schema:place gives such a fact type no place, as its key is two columns; the place compile:ip_place reads it by is the table, the key columns in the objectification`s role order as the one value the instance is named by -- rmap:proj_objkey`s, the components joined by a period -- and the column, and its SELECT (sqlite:pr_src) names the instance as SQLite joins the columns, every one of them filled. Run first with compile:ip_place as schema:place, it answered no place and this answered F.",
DEF("test:np_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("np.md"), A("Plan Name is a value type.\nSlug is a value type.\nAmount is a value type.\nPlan(.Plan Name) is an entity type.\nPlatform API(.Slug) is an entity type.\nPlan includes Platform API.\n  Each Plan, Platform API combination occurs at most once in the population of Plan includes Platform API.\nPlan Product(.id) is an entity type.\nPlan Product objectifies \"Plan includes Platform API\".\nPlan Product has per-call- Amount.\n  Each Plan Product has at most one per-call- Amount.\n"), A("np/np.md"))))),
