"AND A FACT POST, PUT OR DELETE ANSWERS WHAT THE WHOLE CHECK ANSWERS, AND ONLY THE WARNINGS IT ADDED. Over test:w2b_fx, which holds a prohibition already and, as the whole check finds first, no alethic violation, each write answers, byte for byte, what the whole check of its closed store says it owes: a description of a new Function, committed; a new Function named flag, committed with the one prohibition its own derived W2Flag raises; a Function tagged b, refused for the W2Blocked its tag derives; a Function tagged a, committed because the W2Ok its tag derives meets the subset; the flagged Function`s name asserted again, which is how a transition already fired is approved again, committed with nothing added; its name replaced, its name retracted, and the Function itself retracted, each taking the standing prohibition away. And a fact POST over a store already holding an alethic violation answers what the whole check answers, which the gate asks there because the store is not known clean, and is refused only for an alethic violation it adds (test:dirty_gate).",
DEF("test:w2b_gate",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S(A("CONS"), S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("main:alethic_of"), A("ui:violations")), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_post"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("FunctionHasDescription")), K(S2(A("w2b-plain"), A("a fact"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_post"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("FunctionHasName")), K(S2(A("w2b-flag"), A("flag"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_post"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("W2Tag")), K(S2(A("w2b-blocked"), A("b"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_post"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("W2Tag")), K(S2(A("w2b-ok"), A("a"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_post"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("FunctionHasName")), K(S2(A("w2-flag-0"), A("flag"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("FunctionHasName")), K(S2(A("w2-flag-0"), A("plain"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_del"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("FunctionHasName")), K(S2(A("w2-flag-0"), A("flag"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_dele"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("Function")), K(S1(A("w2-flag-0"))))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2b_post"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:w2_fx_bad"), K(A("FunctionHasDescription")), K(S2(A("w2b-plain-2"), A("after a standing violation")))))), A("test:w2b_fx"))),
"THE VERDICT A COMPILE WRITES IS THE ONE THE WHOLE CHECK GIVES. A compile judged the store it wrote in a second process: build.js composed the serve module, booted it on the store and asked main:w2_clean, about 49 s on support. The compile judges it itself, over the closed store it already holds (compile:judge), before the store is put in place: the whole check when the store it replaces is not known clean or its constraints moved (compile:ip_known), and otherwise only the constraints the delta touched, by the argument of the write gate (Thm 1: a constraint that held of the store before and reads no population that moved holds of the store after). Over the clean fixture of test:w2_fx and the dirty one of test:w2_fx_bad, whose Function tagged b derives a W2Blocked its subset refuses: the judge told nothing answers what main:w2_clean answers of each; the judge told the clean store was known clean, given the delta to the dirty one (main:dl_moved, main:w2_types), answers what main:w2_clean answers of the dirty store, F, though the clean store met the subset; and over the clean store with nothing moved it answers T. compile:ip_known answers T only for a recorded alethic_clean T beside the stamp of the same constraints, and F for another stamp, for an F and for no record. compile:vschema, that stamp, is the same over the two fixtures, whose populations differ, and differs between test:w2_fx and the store it extends, whose constraints differ. Before compile:judge was defined it answered F, the subject being guarded for until then.",
"AND THE JUDGE IS THE SQL CHECKS, SO ITS FIXTURES ARE STORES A DATABASE HOLDS. compile:judge reads the database the compile wrote, so each fixture is written to one (test:cvd_db) as a compile writes its tables, and a store a compile writes is closed: test:w2_fx is the composed store with cells added by hand, not closed, and writing it took 18 s a time for its 78 tables, the derived rows of its stored heads absent from them. The fixtures are now one readings file, as test:check_sql`s are: Crate is flagged, allowed, shipped and checked, Crate is blocked fully derived from Crate is flagged, a blocked Crate is allowed and a shipped Crate is checked. The clean store has c1 flagged and allowed and c2 shipped and checked; the dirty store has c1 flagged and not allowed, so it breaks the subset only through what is derived from it, which no table stores and the in-memory judge decides (check:res_sc); and a fourth store has c2 shipped and not checked, which the SQL checks decide: the judge told nothing answers of it what main:w2_clean answers, F. <store> to <the clean fixture, the dirty fixture, the store, the fixture the SQL checks find dirty>.",
DEF("test:cvd_text",
    K(A("Name is a value type.\nCrate(.Name) is an entity type.\nCrate is flagged.\nCrate is allowed.\nCrate is shipped.\nCrate is checked.\nCrate is blocked. *\n* Crate is blocked iff that Crate is flagged.\nIf some Crate is blocked then that Crate is allowed.\nIf some Crate is shipped then that Crate is checked.\n"))),
