"test:judge_scoped holds the judge told the store before was clean to the write gate`s judge. Thm 1: a constraint that held of the store before and reads no population that moved holds of the store after, so the in-memory judge of a write asks only what moved (ui:violations_in), and the SQL checks are scoped the same way: an entry runs when a name it reads is among the fact types that moved, or an object type whose instances it reads is among those whose instances moved (check:scoped), and the rest the in-memory judge is asked is what ui:violations_in asks of it. Over test:cvd_fx`s store the SQL checks find dirty (a shipped Crate not checked) and its store the in-memory judge finds dirty (a blocked Crate not allowed, blocked derived from flagged): told known clean, compile:judge answers of each, given what moved, what null of the alethic part of ui:violations_in answers -- F where what moved reaches the violation, T where it does not -- and told nothing it answers F of both. Run first with compile:judge asking every check whatever moved, it failed.",
