       A("test:cvd_fx")))),
"test:plan_rows holds the plan of the SQL checks to the rows it is stored as. Planning is a function of the schema alone, so a compile plans once and writes the plan beside the Table and Column rows (storage:plan_put: each rendered entry, the names it reads, what the plan covers and the stamp of the constraints it was planned under), and the next judge reads it back (storage:plan_get) and plans again only what the delta touched. The fixture is one readings file, a Crate with a Tag no two Crates share and a Box with exactly one Weight, so Crate and Box are two tables. Its plan written to a database and read back is the same entries and the same cover under the stamp it was written with. A plan written under a stamp is the plan compile:plan_for answers under that stamp with no table touched, entry for entry, even an entry the store would not plan so (each entry`s SQL replaced, so that what is read is told from what is planned); under another stamp it is planned afresh; and with the table Box touched, the entries of what Box carries are planned afresh and every other is read as written. Run first with the plan neither written nor read, it failed.",
