"AN EVENT MOVES A MACHINE ONE TRANSITION, WHEN IT COMES. Over the composed store with a Domain Change at Proposed (test:sp_s0), each event put and stepped (test:sp_ev): (A) a rejection, which only Under Review takes, fires nothing, and the submission after it moves the change to Under Review, where it stays -- the fold over the same two facts, with no row placing the machine, reads Rejected, firing the rejection once the submission reached its source; (B) a revision returns it to Proposed, and the submission posted again, a fact the store already holds, moves it to Under Review once more (store:step_held), while a fact the store does not hold leaves the store as it was; (C) an approval before the change is evaluated fires nothing, its guard unmet, and evaluating it afterwards moves nothing either, though the guard then holds: a guard is read when its event comes. Seen to fail with store:step_closed answering its closed store unstepped: (A) read Rejected. The store a fact it does not hold leaves as it was is compared with itself, taken once: a move records its cause at the clock`s time, so two takings of the same writes differ by their times.",
"<store>: <a1, a2, b3, b4, c5, c6 o c5>, each store of test:status_step taken once from the one before it. The law, each of these a DEF of its own, named b3 four times, b4 twice and c5 three times, and each of them stepped every store before it again: 41 steps where 6 are the law, about a third of the whole report. [f o g, g] = [f o 1, 1] o [g, id] threads each store to the next.",
