            S3(A("PhHas"), S2(A("Thing"), A("Code")), S3(A("proj"), A("PhSource"), S2(N(1), N(2)))),
            S3(A("PhDropped"), S1(A("Thing")), S3(A("proj"), S4(A("sel"), A("PhHas"), N(2), A("drop")), S1(N(1)))),
            S3(A("PhFresh"), S1(A("Thing")), S3(A("proj"), S4(A("sel"), A("PhHas"), N(2), A("fresh")), S1(N(1)))))))))),
"AN ENTERED VALUE OVERRIDES THE DERIVED ONE, AND A RULE READING THE HEAD SEES ONLY THE ENTERED ONE (for a + head). Over test:ph_store, closed by derive:closed, PhHas holds t1 keep, which is asserted, and t2 fresh, which is derived. It does not hold t1 drop, which its rule derives against t1`s entered value. PhDropped is empty, because no PhHas a rule could read says drop, and PhFresh is t2. derive:sm_one merged a + head against its asserted rows only after the fixpoint, so a rule that read the head during the fixpoint saw both values: PhDropped held t1. test:semi_move is the same failure over a machine`s status.",
