"AN EVENT THAT NUDGES A GAUGE FIRES ITS MACHINE AND PERFORMS ITS STEP. Over test:dft_fx, a write asserting LawPing of law-ping, a classified fact type, records its Event, whose closure derives LawMoves and LawNudges of law-gauge; LawNudges triggers law-nudge, a self-loop at law-drifting of the machine Law Drift, which is for Gauge. After the write law-gauge is at 0.2, its rest 0 plus 0.8 of no displacement plus the move 0.2, as law step performs step:settle; and an Event of LawNudges caused law-nudge in sm.law-gauge. LawNudges is declared by its reading only, as a fact type derived and stored is. Seen to fail (drift-step -> F) with the step taken before the Events were recorded, and the attempt asking the status of an object type named by the machine, Law Drift, which none is: law-gauge stayed at 0 and nothing was caused; and again with those two fixed and the players of LawNudges read from state:declared and state:schemereadings only: the cause was recorded and law-gauge stayed at 0, step:settle sent no move.",
DEF("test:drift_step",
    S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dft_moved"), A("test:dft_caused"))), A("test:dft_written"))),
"The rows the catch-up fixture adds to the gauge fixture, each <fact type, row>: LawPing2 pushes law-gauge by -0.5; and three Events that reached law-gauge before anything consumed them, as on a store written before writes recorded causes, each of a pushing type, at its time, moving law-gauge and reaching it: law-e3 of LawPing at 19:00:00, which a cause already names in the form a write records, the trigger fact as an Event at the write`s time; law-e1 of LawPing at 19:52:01; and law-e2 of LawPing2 at 20:09:06. Each row is put before the store`s population, so LawNudges holds law-e2, law-e1, law-e3, which is not their order in time. And the shape of the verb replay as resolution.md declares it, row-and-cells to outcome-and-store, which the composed store holds only once its carriers are compiled from that file again.",
DEF("test:cu_rows",
    K(S(
       S2(A("FunctionAcceptsTypeExpression"), S2(A("replay"), A("row-and-cells"))),
