       S2(A("EventOccurredAtTimestamp"), S2(A("LawNudges:1=law-e3|2=law-gauge@2026-10-06T19:00:01Z"), A("2026-10-06T19:00:01Z"))),
       S2(A("EventCausedTransitionInStateMachine"), S3(A("LawNudges:1=law-e3|2=law-gauge@2026-10-06T19:00:01Z"), A("law-nudge"), A("sm.law-gauge"))),
       S2(A("EventIsOfEventType"), S2(A("law-e1"), A("LawPing"))),
       S2(A("EventOccurredAtTimestamp"), S2(A("law-e1"), A("2026-10-06T19:52:01Z"))),
       S2(A("LawMoves"), S3(A("law-e1"), A("law-gauge"), A("0.2"))),
       S2(A("LawNudges"), S2(A("law-e1"), A("law-gauge"))),
       S2(A("EventIsOfEventType"), S2(A("law-e2"), A("LawPing2"))),
       S2(A("EventOccurredAtTimestamp"), S2(A("law-e2"), A("2026-10-06T20:09:06Z"))),
       S2(A("LawMoves"), S3(A("law-e2"), A("law-gauge"), A("-0.5"))),
       S2(A("LawNudges"), S2(A("law-e2"), A("law-gauge")))))),
"The subset constraint instances.md declares over Event caused Transition in State Machine, as the composed store carries it in state:setcmp: if some Event caused some Transition in some State Machine then that Event is of some Event Type where that Transition is triggered by that Event Type. A violation of it is named by its first span, EventIsInvolvedInEventCausedTransitionInStateMachine.",
