DEF("test:lambda_path",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("implode"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("")), S3(A("CONS"), A("module:root"), K(A("/arest")))))),
"A COMPILED CACHE STAMPED FOR A DIFFERENT LAMBDA IS NOT USED. The compiled carrier holds the relational map as stored:rmap:X cells, and each rmap:X reads stored:rmap:X before it derives; its stamp AREST_COMPILED_FROM was the digest of the design-state text alone, so after a change to lambda`s relational map a cache written by the old lambda still matched, was spliced, and overrode the new rmap:X DEFs. The stamp is now the first sixteen hex digits of the SHA-256 of the lambda text followed by the design-state text, and build.js, the reader, declines a carrier whose stamp is not that of the lambda and design-state it composes. Three checks, over literal texts. The stamp a cache written by lambda law-lambda over schema law-schema carries is 5a9ccd070a7384d0, the SHA-256 of law-lambdalaw-schema, which is what build.js computes from those two files read in that order. compile:stamped, the writer, stamps schema law-schema with compile:stamp of this module`s lambda text followed by law-schema. And that stamp is not the one law-lambda wrote, so the reader declines that cache and lambda derives the map. Run before the writer read lambda, it failed (compiled-lambda-keyed -> F): the stamp was compile:stamp of law-schema alone. What this cannot hold is build.js itself, which runs before any lambda does; it is held by the first check, which pins the digest it computes, and by the second, which pins the order of the texts it reads.",
DEF("test:compiled_keyed",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp"), K(A("law-lambdalaw-schema"))), K(A("5a9ccd070a7384d0")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), N(5), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamped"), K(S7(A("law-1"), A("law-2"), A("law-3"), A("law-schema"), A("law-5"), A("law-6"), A("law-7"))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamp"), S3(A("COMP"), A("implode"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("")), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("fs:read"), A("test:lambda_path")), K(A("law-schema")))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("not"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), N(5), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:stamped"), K(S7(A("law-1"), A("law-2"), A("law-3"), A("law-schema"), A("law-5"), A("law-6"), A("law-7"))))),
          K(A("5a9ccd070a7384d0")))))))),
