"A RETRACT OF A ROW A PROJECTION DERIVES RETRACTS ITS ONE SOURCE. A derived fact is specifically meant for views, otherwise the direct facts would do, and a retract of a derivation retracts its source facts. Over test:drd_fx, LawDrdHas is derived and stored as the projection of LawDrdIn on its Function, and law-drd-f1 is in law-drd-d1 alone: a fact DELETE of law-drd-f1 in LawDrdHas commits (201), after which LawDrdIn holds law-drd-f1 in law-drd-d1 no longer, LawDrdHas no longer holds law-drd-f1 and still holds law-drd-f2, and LawDrdIn holds the two rows of law-drd-f2 and no other. Before main:dr_plan the retract took the head row alone, and the source stayed.",
