       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(N(201)))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(A("law-drd-f1"), A("law-drd-d1")))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdHas"), S1(A("law-drd-f1")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:drd_holds"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdHas"), S1(A("law-drd-f2")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:drd_only"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(A("LawDrdIn"), S2(S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d2")), S2(A("law-drd-f2"), A("law-drd-d3")))))))),
       A("test:drd_ra")))),
"A RETRACT OF A ROW A JOIN DERIVES ALONG ONE PATH RETRACTS THE ASSERTED FACTS ON THAT PATH (the rule: a row derived through a join retracts every asserted fact on its derivation path that no other derivation of the same row survives without). Over test:drd_fx, law-drd-f1 is under law-drd-e1 along one path, law-drd-f1 in law-drd-d1 and law-drd-d1 under law-drd-e1: a fact DELETE of that row of LawDrdUnder commits (201), after which LawDrdIn holds law-drd-f1 in law-drd-d1 no longer, LawDrdSub holds law-drd-d1 under law-drd-e1 no longer, LawDrdUnder no longer holds law-drd-f1 under law-drd-e1 and still holds law-drd-f2 under law-drd-e2, and LawDrdIn and LawDrdSub hold their other two rows each and no other. Before main:dr_plan the retract took the head row alone, and both sources stayed.",
