    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvView"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvView")))), A("id"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvKept"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvKept")))), A("id"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvEntered"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvEntered")))), A("id"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S4(A("item"), A("LawNvSaid"), PHI(), S1(A("LawNvSaid")))), A("id")))))),
"<<store, resource>, methods> to T when the perspectives the map offers the resource over the store are those methods.",
DEF("test:nvm_offers",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("nav:perspectives"), N(1)), N(2)))),
"THE CONTROLS THE MAP OFFERS FOLLOW THE MARKER. links(e) = nav(e) union transitions(status(e)) offers per fact type what its derivation marker admits: an asserted fact type GET, POST, PUT and DELETE; a head derived on query (*) or derived and stored (**) GET, and a DELETE that retracts the facts its row is derived from, and no POST or PUT, since its rule owns its rows; a semi-derived head (+ or ++) GET, and POST, PUT and DELETE on the values entered, a DELETE restoring the derived default. And a head derived on query is a view group in the menu: its own collection link, read-only, though no table holds it. Over test:nvm_fx: nav:perspectives offers LawNvSaid GET, POST, PUT and DELETE, LawNvView and LawNvKept GET and DELETE, and LawNvEntered GET, POST, PUT and DELETE; the actions of the collection page at LawNvView hold no Add, and those at Function hold its Add as before; and the root at no App lists LawNvView as an item and none of the other three. Expected before the change to fail (nav-markers -> F): the map named every method of http:method_kinds for every resource, every collection page offered Add, and the root listed only the tables of the relational map.",
DEF("test:nav_markers",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("COMP"), S8(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvSaid"))), K(S4(A("GET"), A("POST"), A("PUT"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvView"))), K(S2(A("GET"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvKept"))), K(S2(A("GET"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_offers"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawNvEntered"))), K(S4(A("GET"), A("POST"), A("PUT"), A("DELETE"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:coll_actions"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S1(A("LawNvView"))))), K(S2(A("actions"), A(""))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:coll_actions"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S1(A("Function"))))), K(S3(A("actions"), A(""), S4(A("button"), A("+ new"), S2(A("new"), A("Function")), A("Add")))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:nvm_menu"), A("test:nvm_root"))),
       A("test:nvm_fx")))),
"A FULLY DERIVED HEAD IS A VIEW. CLAUDE.md, the application flow: a derived fact type is a view. test:derived_view reads one literal readings file through compile:check, as test:local_names does: Member joins Club and Club holds Venue are asserted, each many to many, and Member attends Venue is marked * and derived by joining the two. Over the store those cells make, the relational map lays out no table for the head and rmap:ddl emits CREATE VIEW for it; and through the storage interface -- storage:fresh, storage:schema, storage:put of compile:tables, then storage:columns and storage:rows of the head -- the view answers exactly the rows derive:on_read derives, which are not none. The database is law-derived-view.db beside the process, made fresh before and cleared after.",
DEF("test:dv_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("views.md"), A("Member(.id) is an entity type.\nClub(.id) is an entity type.\nVenue(.id) is an entity type.\nMember joins Club.\n  Each Member, Club combination occurs at most once in the population of Member joins Club.\nClub holds Venue.\n  Each Club, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Club holds Venue.\nMember attends Venue. *\n  Each Member, Venue combination occurs at most once in the population of Member attends Venue.\n* Member attends Venue iff Member joins Club and that Club holds Venue.\nMember 'ann' joins Club 'chess'.\nMember 'cy' joins Club 'chess'.\nMember 'bob' joins Club 'go'.\nClub 'chess' holds Venue 'york'.\nClub 'chess' holds Venue 'leeds'.\nClub 'go' holds Venue 'hull'.\nClub 'rowing' holds Venue 'ely'.\n"), A("fx/views.md"))))),
"The store test:dv_files makes: the cells compile:check answers for it, each chunked as a compile files it (compile:cellify).",
