"<store, database, counts> to <store, database, tables, head rows>.",
DEF("test:dv_s4",
    S5(A("CONS"), N(1), N(2), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:tables"), N(2)), A("test:dv_rows"))),
"<store, database, tables, head rows> to <store, tables, head rows, database>, the database cleared.",
DEF("test:dv_s5",
    S5(A("CONS"), N(1), N(3), N(4), S3(A("COMP"), A("storage:fresh"), N(2)))),
"<store, ...> to the rows the derivation derives for the head.",
DEF("test:dv_derived",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("derive:on_read"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dv_head"), N(1)))),
"<store, tables, head rows, database> to T when the database holds no table of the head, the script creates a view of it, the derivation derives some rows of it, and the view answers exactly those.",
DEF("test:dv_verdict",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S5(A("CONS"),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:dv_head"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), N(2)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("cn:contains"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("schema:ddl"), N(1)), K(A("CREATE VIEW \"MemberAttendsVenue\"")))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("null"), A("test:dv_derived")),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(3), A("test:dv_derived")))))),
DEF("test:derived_view",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("test:dv_verdict"), S6(A("COMP"), A("test:dv_s5"), A("test:dv_s4"), A("test:dv_s3"), A("test:dv_s2"), A("test:dv_s1")), A("test:dv_store"))),
"<store>: transitions of one event, <from, event, to>, with no guards: c1 to cT and cT to pDone, a to b and b to c, x to y and y to x.",
DEF("test:sc_trs",
    K(S6(S3(A("c1"), A("e"), A("cT")), S3(A("cT"), A("e"), A("pDone")), S3(A("a"), A("e"), A("b")), S3(A("b"), A("e"), A("c")), S3(A("x"), A("e"), A("y")), S3(A("y"), A("e"), A("x"))))),
"A SUB-MACHINE THAT ENDS CARRIES ITS EVENT ON. test:step_completes holds store:sc_run to test:sc_trs over the composed store, the ends being cT, x and y. From cT, which ends a sub-machine, the event goes on to pDone; from b, which ends nothing, it stays at b; from y it goes on to x and stops there, since x would take it back to y, where it stood. Run first with no Status counted an end, it failed (step-completes -> F).",
DEF("test:step_completes",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_run"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("law-e")), K(A("cT")), A("id"), A("test:sc_trs"), K(S3(A("cT"), A("x"), A("y"))))), K(A("pDone")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_run"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("law-e")), K(A("b")), A("id"), A("test:sc_trs"), K(S3(A("cT"), A("x"), A("y"))))), K(A("b")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_run"), S6(A("CONS"), K(A("law-e")), K(A("y")), A("id"), A("test:sc_trs"), K(S3(A("cT"), A("x"), A("y"))))), K(A("x"))))))),
"<store>: the composed store with a sub-machine law-open of law-sr defining law-received, which law-accept exits there, and law-merged, which only law-sr`s law-close exits. The Status law-open of law-sr has the sub-machine law-open (Status has sub-machine State Machine Definition), the one name for the composite and the machine.",
DEF("test:ea_fx",
    S8(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-open"), A("law-open"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("TransitionExitsStatusInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S3(A("law-close"), A("law-merged"), A("law-sr"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("TransitionExitsStatusInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S3(A("law-accept"), A("law-received"), A("law-open"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StatusIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-open"), A("law-sr"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StatusIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-received"), A("law-open"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StatusIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("law-merged"), A("law-open"))))),
       A("id"))),
"A STATUS ENDS A SUB-MACHINE WHEN NOTHING OF THE SUB-MACHINE LEAVES IT. test:end_at holds store:sc_end_at over test:ea_fx: law-merged ends law-open, which law-sr defines and which nothing exits it in; law-received does not, law-accept exiting it in law-open; and law-open, a Status of law-sr, ends nothing, law-sr being the sub-machine of no Status. Run first with every machine counted a sub-machine, it failed (end-at -> F), law-open answering.",
DEF("test:end_at",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("law-merged")), A("test:ea_fx"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("law-received")), A("test:ea_fx"))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("law-open")), A("test:ea_fx")))))),
"A MACHINE IS A STATUS ONLY BY NESTING. State machines must be defined correctly. state.md read `State Machine Definition is a subtype of Status`, so every machine was a Status, and a top-level one, which no Transition reaches, stood against core.md`s `For each Status, some Transition is from that Status or some Transition is to that Status`. It reads now `Status has sub-machine State Machine Definition`, each State Machine Definition the sub-machine of at most one Status. test:sub_machine holds the reader and the machine over test:sm_files, a literal readings file: Ticket, a top-level machine whose Status Open has the sub-machine Review, where approve takes Draft to Approved, and Note, another top-level machine. The reader files Open has sub-machine Review with the uniqueness on the role of the machine; no machine is among the Statuses; the inclusive-or the file states is read, and every Status is the from or the to of some Transition. Approved ends a sub-machine, the end of Review, and neither Draft, which approve leaves there, nor Closed nor Read, Statuses of top-level machines, does (store:sc_end_at); entering Open enters Draft (main:enter); the machine for Ticket nests Review and not Note (main:noun_smds_all), and resolve, which leaves Open, leaves Draft and Approved too (main:machine_trs). Run first, with lambda reading a machine as a Status of the same name, it failed (sub-machine -> F): Approved ended nothing, Open entered itself, and Ticket nested nothing.",
DEF("test:sm_files",
    K(S1(S3(A("sm.md"), A("Status(.Name) is an entity type.\nState Machine Definition(.Name) is an entity type.\nTransition(.Name) is an entity type.\nEvent Type(.Name) is an entity type.\nObject Type(.Name) is an entity type.\nObject Type Instance(.Name) is an entity type.\nName is a value type.\n\nObject Type Instance is instance of Object Type.\nState Machine Definition is for Object Type.\nStatus has sub-machine State Machine Definition.\n  For each State Machine Definition, at most one Status has sub-machine that State Machine Definition.\nStatus is initial in State Machine Definition.\nStatus is defined in State Machine Definition.\nTransition is defined in State Machine Definition.\nTransition is from- Status.\nTransition is to- Status.\nTransition is triggered by Event Type.\nTransition exits Status in State Machine Definition.\n\nFor each Status, some Transition is from that Status or some Transition is to that Status.\n\nState Machine Definition 'Ticket' is for Object Type 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Open' is initial in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Open' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Closed' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nTransition 'resolve' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nTransition 'resolve' is from Status 'Open'.\nTransition 'resolve' is to Status 'Closed'.\nTransition 'resolve' is triggered by Event Type 'Resolves'.\nTransition 'resolve' exits Status 'Open' in State Machine Definition 'Ticket'.\nStatus 'Open' has sub-machine State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nStatus 'Draft' is initial in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nStatus 'Draft' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nStatus 'Approved' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nTransition 'approve' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nTransition 'approve' is from Status 'Draft'.\nTransition 'approve' is to Status 'Approved'.\nTransition 'approve' is triggered by Event Type 'Approves'.\nTransition 'approve' exits Status 'Draft' in State Machine Definition 'Review'.\nState Machine Definition 'Note' is for Object Type 'Note'.\nStatus 'Unread' is initial in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nStatus 'Unread' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nStatus 'Read' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nTransition 'read' is defined in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\nTransition 'read' is from Status 'Unread'.\nTransition 'read' is to Status 'Read'.\nTransition 'read' is triggered by Event Type 'Reads'.\nTransition 'read' exits Status 'Unread' in State Machine Definition 'Note'.\n"), A("smx/sm.md"))))),
"<any>: the cells compile:check answers for test:sm_files, as a store (test:ln_store).",
DEF("test:sm_cells",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:ln_store"),
       S4(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("compile:of_x"), A("compile:findings_of_x")), A("compile:x"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), A("test:ln_pair")), A("test:sm_files"))))),
"<cells>: the cells with each fact type`s rows as a population cell of its own, where a machine reads them (system:pop_rows).",
DEF("test:sm_store_of",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("CONS"), K(A("CELL")), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), N(5)))), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:fts")), A("id")))),
       A("id")))),
"<cells, store> to the Statuses the readings populate: the instances Object Type Instance is instance of Object Type gives Status (state:otpops is gone; the instance list of a type is a view of the classification, and test:sm_files declares the classification so the reader reflects it, as instances.md does for an app).",
DEF("test:sm_statuses",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Status")))), S2(A("CONS"), N(1)), K(PHI()))), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType")), N(2)))))),
"<cells, store> to the rows <from, event, to> the machine for Ticket fires, with the machines nested in it.",
DEF("test:sm_trs",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("main:machine_trs"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Ticket"))))),
DEF("test:sub_machine",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"),
       S(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:seteq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition")), N(2))), K(S1(S2(A("Open"), A("Review")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("UC:in:StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition#2")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:ucs")), N(1)))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Ticket"), A("Note"), A("Review"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Ticket"), A("Note"), A("Review"))), A("test:sm_statuses")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("DJ:e:TransitionIsFromStatus#2+TransitionIsToStatus#2")), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("ast:fetch"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("state:djmands")), N(1)))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("null"), S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:setminus"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:sm_statuses"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("cat"), S3(A("CONS"),
                S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("TransitionIsFromStatus")), N(2)))),
                S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(2)), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("TransitionIsToStatus")), N(2))))))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Open")), A("test:sm_statuses"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Approved")), N(2))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Draft")), N(2))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Closed")), N(2))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("store:sc_end_at"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Read")), N(2))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:enter"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Open")), N(2))), K(A("Draft")))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Review")), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:noun_smds_all"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Ticket")))))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("Note")), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:noun_smds_all"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(A("Ticket")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Draft"), A("Resolves"), A("Closed"))), A("test:sm_trs"))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("Approved"), A("Resolves"), A("Closed"))), A("test:sm_trs")))),
       S3(A("COMP"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), A("test:sm_store_of")), A("test:sm_cells")))),
"A VALUE THE READINGS ENUMERATE IS ONE THEY INTRODUCE. test:enum_introduces holds compile:ip_gone over literal rows: of the instances the last readings introduced (law ep, law-i0, law-i1), the new readings introduce law-i1 by an instance sentence and law ep as one of a value type`s possible values, so law-i0 alone is gone. Run first with compile:ip_r1typed reading instance sentences only, it failed (enum-introduces -> F), law ep answering gone.",
DEF("test:enum_introduces",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("compile:ip_gone"), K(S3(S3(A("law ep"), A("law-i0"), A("law-i1")), PHI(), S2(S2(A("ObjectTypeHasEnumValues"), S2(A("law-kind"), A("'law-other', 'law ep'"))), S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S2(A("law-i1"), A("law-t"))))))), K(S1(A("law-i0")))))),
"<store>: the composed store with c-law-rc and c-law-rc2 instances of Constraint, as a create files them (state:otpops), which an obligation over Constraint reads (ui:ids).",
DEF("test:rc_reg",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cls_put"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(S2(A("c-law-rc"), A("Constraint")), S2(A("c-law-rc2"), A("Constraint"))))))),
