    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("ConstraintSpan"), A("deontic"), A("c-law-rc"))), A("id"))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S3(A("ConstraintSpan"), A("deontic"), A("c-law-rc2"))), A("id"))))),
       A("test:rc_deo"))),
"<store>: the facts the retract of the Constraint Span c-law-rc2.r-law-rc3, by its own id, removes from test:rc_fx.",
DEF("test:rc_c",
    S3(A("COMP"), N(1), S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_entity"), S3(A("CONS"), A("test:rc_fx"), K(A("c-law-rc2.r-law-rc3")))))),
"<fact type, facts>: the rows of every entry of the fact type among the facts a retract removed, which names a fact type once for each id it retracted.",
DEF("test:rc_rows",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("theta:flatten"), S2(A("ALPHA"), S4(A("COND"), S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(1), N(2)), N(1))), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(2)), K(PHI()))), A("distl"))),
"<the answer of test:rc_a, the facts of test:rc_b, the facts of test:rc_c>: what test:retract_cascade says of each.",
DEF("test:rc_checks",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), K(N(201)))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("sm.dc-law-step")), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("StateMachineIsCurrentlyInStatus")), S3(A("COMP"), N(3), N(1)))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc"), A("UC"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintIsOfConstraintType")), N(2))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc2"), A("UC"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintIsOfConstraintType")), N(2))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc"), A("r-law-rc"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintSpan")), N(2))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc2"), A("r-law-rc"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintSpan")), N(2))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc.r-law-rc"), N(1))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintSpanHasPosition")), N(2))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc2"), A("r-law-rc3"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintSpan")), N(3))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc2.r-law-rc3"), N(1))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintSpanHasPosition")), N(3))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc2"), A("r-law-rc"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintSpan")), N(3))))),
       S4(A("COMP"), A("not"), A("theta:member"), S3(A("CONS"), K(S2(A("c-law-rc2"), A("UC"))), S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ConstraintIsOfConstraintType")), N(3)))))))),
"A RETRACT TAKES WHAT CANNOT STAND WITHOUT IT, AND LEAVES WHAT ONLY REFERRED TO IT (main:retract_entity). Over the composed store: (A) the Domain Change dc-law-step, its status stored at Under Review by its submission, is retracted, and the write commits (201) with no row of State Machine is currently in Status left for its machine; (B) two Constraints span one Role, c-law-rc no other and c-law-rc2 another as well, and the Role`s retract takes both spans over it, and each span`s Position with its span, since an objectified instance is its fact (main:rc_objs), but neither Constraint. A constraint has multiple spans because of subsets, equality, other comparators, etc. A constraint with unfilled roles gets a deontic warning, but it`s valid to want to keep the constraint and span it across different roles after a delete. So Each Constraint spans some Role is an obligation (core.md), and c-law-rc stays, spanning none, which the obligation warns of (test:rc_warned); (C) the span c-law-rc2.r-law-rc3, retracted by its own id, takes its pair and its Position, and leaves its Constraint and the Constraint`s other span (main:re_own). Seen to fail with main:rc_mach answering none (the support.auto.dev refusal, StateMachineIsCurrentlyInStatus subset), with main:rc_mand answering none, with the mandatory still alethic (the Role`s retract took c-law-rc`s Constraint Type), with main:rc_objs answering none (the Role`s retract left both spans` Positions) and with main:re_own answering none (the span retracted by its id kept its pair).",
DEF("test:retract_cascade",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rc_checks"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:rc_a"), A("test:rc_b"), A("test:rc_c")))),
