    S4(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus")), K(S2(A("dc-law-step"), A("Under Review"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sp_put"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("StateMachineIsInstanceOfStateMachineDefinition")), K(S2(A("sm.dc-law-step"), A("Domain Change"))))),
       A("test:sp_a2"))),
"A RETRACT LEAVES NO ROW OF THE ENTITY IN A HEAD THE STORE KEEPS (main:re_names). Over test:rd_fx, the entity DELETE of dc-law-step answers 201, and neither ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus holds a row of dc-law-step nor StateMachineIsInstanceOfStateMachineDefinition one of sm.dc-law-step: the rows a retract on support.auto.dev can leave behind. Seen to fail with main:re_names answering the declared fact types alone.",
DEF("test:retract_derived",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(N(201)))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("dc-law-step")), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsCurrentlyInStatus")), N(3))))),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("null"), A("solve:assoc"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("sm.dc-law-step")), S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("StateMachineIsInstanceOfStateMachineDefinition")), N(3))))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_entity_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:rd_fx"), K(A("Function")), K(S1(A("dc-law-step"))))))),
"<store>: the composed store with a schema shaped as instances.md`s classification: LawSdrIn, a Function an instance of a Description, and LawSdrSub, a Description a subtype of another, asserted; LawSdrProper, derived and stored, a Function properly of each supertype of a Description it is an instance of; and LawSdrMost, derived and stored, its instances less its proper ones. law-sdr-1 and law-sdr-2 are Functions.",
DEF("test:sdr_schema",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
             S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
                K(S2(A("state:fts"), S4(
                   S5(A("LawSdrIn"), S2(A("Function"), A("Description")), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), PHI(), S1(PHI())),
                   S5(A("LawSdrSub"), S2(A("Description"), A("Description")), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), PHI(), S1(PHI())),
                   S5(A("LawSdrProper"), S2(A("Function"), A("Description")), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), PHI(), S1(PHI())),
                   S5(A("LawSdrMost"), S2(A("Function"), A("Description")), S1(S2(N(1), N(2))), PHI(), S1(PHI()))))))),
             K(S2(A("state:declared"), S2(
                S2(A("LawSdrIn"), S2(A("Function"), A("Description"))),
                S2(A("LawSdrSub"), S2(A("Description"), A("Description")))))))),
          K(S2(A("state:derived"), S2(S2(A("LawSdrProper"), A("derived-and-stored")), S2(A("LawSdrMost"), A("derived-and-stored"))))))),
       K(S2(A("state:rules"), S2(
          S3(A("LawSdrProper"), S2(A("Function"), A("Description")), S3(A("proj"), S4(A("join"), A("LawSdrIn"), A("LawSdrSub"), S3(N(1), N(2), N(3))), S2(N(1), N(3)))),
          S3(A("LawSdrMost"), S2(A("Function"), A("Description")), S3(A("minus"), A("LawSdrIn"), A("LawSdrProper"))))))))),
"<store>: the store with law-sdr-1 and law-sdr-2 Functions, as a create files them (state:otpops).",
DEF("test:sdr_reg",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:cls_put"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(S2(S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Function")), S2(A("law-sdr-2"), A("Function"))))))),
"The asserted rows of the fixture, each <fact type, row>: law-sdr-1 an instance of Response and of Message, law-sdr-2 of Message, and Response a subtype of Message.",
DEF("test:sdr_rows",
    K(S4(
       S2(A("LawSdrIn"), S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Response"))),
       S2(A("LawSdrIn"), S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Message"))),
       S2(A("LawSdrIn"), S2(A("law-sdr-2"), A("Message"))),
       S2(A("LawSdrSub"), S2(A("Response"), A("Message")))))),
"<store>: the fixture, its rows put over its schema and closed from it as a write closes, so it holds what its two derived and stored heads derive.",
DEF("test:sdr_fx",
    S3(A("COMP"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("store:closed_from"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"), S4(A("COMP"), S2(A("INSERT"), A("test:dft_put")), A("apndr"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), A("reverse"), A("test:sdr_rows")), A("id"))))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sdr_reg"), A("test:sdr_schema")))),
"<store> to the rows it holds of LawSdrProper and of LawSdrMost.",
