       S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawSdrProper")), A("id"))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("system:pop_rows"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("LawSdrMost")), A("id"))))),
"<<body, status, store>, proper rows, most rows> to T when the write committed (201) and the store it made holds those rows of LawSdrProper and LawSdrMost and no other.",
DEF("test:sdr_held",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), S4(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S3(A("COMP"), N(2), N(1)), K(N(201)))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S5(A("COMP"), N(1), A("test:sdr_pops"), N(3), N(1)), N(2))),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), S5(A("COMP"), N(2), A("test:sdr_pops"), N(3), N(1)), N(3)))))),
"<store> to what a fact DELETE of law-sdr-1 as an instance of Response answers.",
DEF("test:sdr_ra",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("LawSdrIn")), K(S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Response")))))),
"<store> to what an entity DELETE of the Function law-sdr-2 answers.",
DEF("test:sdr_rb",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("main:retract_entity_step"), S4(A("CONS"), A("id"), K(A("Function")), K(S1(A("law-sdr-2")))))),
"A RETRACT TAKES BACK WHAT A STORED DERIVATION DERIVED FROM IT. `**` columns store the derivation and updates, but do not accept overrides, and retracting a fact is just writing a null to the columns related to that fact. A `**` head is derived on update (Halpin and Morgan 2008, pp. 100-101): stored, and recomputed whenever its defining facts change, a retraction included. Over test:sdr_fx, whose LawSdrProper and LawSdrMost are derived and stored from the asserted LawSdrIn and LawSdrSub as instances.md derives Object Type Instance is properly of and is most specifically of Object Type: the closure holds law-sdr-1 properly of Message and most specifically of Response, and law-sdr-2 most specifically of Message; (A) a fact DELETE of law-sdr-1 as an instance of Response commits, after which law-sdr-1 is properly of nothing and most specifically of Message, and law-sdr-2 is still most specifically of Message; (B) an entity DELETE of law-sdr-2 commits, after which law-sdr-2 is most specifically of nothing, and law-sdr-1 keeps both its rows.",
DEF("test:stored_retract",
    S4(A("COMP"), A("fp:and_all"), A("test:sdr_checks"), A("test:sdr_fx"))),
"<fixture> to the four verdicts of test:stored_retract.",
DEF("test:sdr_checks",
       S5(A("CONS"),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(1), K(S1(S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Message"))))), A("test:sdr_pops")),
          S4(A("COMP"), A("test:rows_eq"), S3(A("CONS"), N(2), K(S2(S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Response")), S2(A("law-sdr-2"), A("Message"))))), A("test:sdr_pops")),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sdr_held"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:sdr_ra"), K(PHI()), K(S2(S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Message")), S2(A("law-sdr-2"), A("Message")))))),
          S3(A("COMP"), A("test:sdr_held"), S4(A("CONS"), A("test:sdr_rb"), K(S1(S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Message")))), K(S1(S2(A("law-sdr-1"), A("Response")))))))),
"<store>: the composed store with Observation is of Fact declared, each Observation of at most one Fact, as support.auto.dev declares it.",
DEF("test:br_schema",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"),
       S3(A("COMP"), A("test:w2_ext"), S3(A("CONS"), A("id"),
          K(S2(A("state:fts"), S1(S5(A("ObservationIsOfFact"), S2(A("Observation"), A("Fact")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S1(PHI()))))))),
       K(S2(A("state:declared"), S1(S2(A("ObservationIsOfFact"), S2(A("Observation"), A("Fact"))))))))),
"<store>: test:br_schema with Observation and Fact entity types, three Observations obs-law-br1, obs-law-br2 and obs-law-br3 and two Facts filed as a create files them, and the first two Observations each of one Fact.",
DEF("test:br_fx",
    S7(A("COMP"),
